2025-12-18T10:27:44.178Z [iterm2] [info] Message from server: {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":4,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"success\":true,\"file_path\":\"/Users/happyhawking/Documents/Projects/Current/writer/specs.md\",\"content\":\"# Oral History Book Research System\\n\\n## Specification Document v1.0\\n\\nA CLI tool for managing WWII oral history transcripts, designed for book research. Veterans are first-class citizens - every search, every passage, every insight stays connected to the person who lived it.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Core Concepts\\n\\n### 1.1 The Veteran (Primary Entity)\\n\\nThe veteran is the central organizing principle. They are characters in your book, not just metadata on a transcript.\\n\\n```\\nVETERAN\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 identity (name, unit, rank, service dates)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 timeline (events, ordered chronologically)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 relationships (people they mention)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 transcript (Q&A responses)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 responses[]\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 text (interviewer question + veteran answer)\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 extracted metadata (LLM-generated)\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 paragraphs[] (for precise search)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 notes (your writer annotations)\\n```\\n\\n### 1.2 The Response (Atomic Unit of Testimony)\\n\\nA response is one interviewer question paired with the veteran's complete answer. This is the natural unit of oral history - one topic, one narrative block.\\n\\nResponses are never split arbitrarily. They may contain multiple paragraphs (for search precision), but retrieval always returns the full response.\\n\\n### 1.3 The Paragraph (Search Precision Layer)\\n\\nParagraphs exist only for embedding/search. When a search hits a paragraph, the system returns its parent response. You never see orphaned paragraphs.\\n\\n### 1.4 Annotations (Your Writer's Layer)\\n\\nAnnotations are your notes, chapter assignments, and flags. They attach to responses but live separately - source material is immutable, your interpretation is mutable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. File Structure\\n\\n```\\noralhistory/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 .git/                          # Version control\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 config.yaml                    # System configuration\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 veterans/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 {veteran_id}.yaml          # One file per veteran (profile + transcript)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 annotations/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 {veteran_id}.yaml          # Your notes per veteran\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 index/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 embeddings.sqlite          # Vector search (SQLite + sqlite-vss)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 relationships.sqlite       # Cross-veteran connections\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 exports/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 {export_name}.md           # Generated exports\\n```\\n\\n### 2.1 Why This Structure\\n\\n- **YAML for veterans**: Human-readable, git-diffable, editable by hand if needed\\n- **Separate annotations**: Your work distinct from source material\\n- **SQLite for indexes**: Fast search, embeddings, no external dependencies\\n- **Git-backed**: Every change tracked, undo anything\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Data Models\\n\\n### 3.1 Veteran File (`veterans/{veteran_id}.yaml`)\\n\\n```yaml\\n# veterans/girusi_hugo.yaml\\n\\nid: girusi_hugo\\nname: \\\"Hugo Girusi\\\"\\nunit: \\\"603rd Tank Destroyer Battalion\\\"\\nrank: \\\"Staff Sergeant\\\"\\nservice_dates:\\n  start: \\\"1941\\\"\\n  end: \\\"1945\\\"\\n\\n# LLM-synthesized from transcript\\ntimeline:\\n  - date: \\\"1941\\\"\\n    date_precision: \\\"year\\\"  # year | month | day | approximate\\n    event: \\\"Enlisted at Fort Lewis\\\"\\n    confidence: \\\"inferred\\\"  # stated | inferred | approximate\\n    response_ids: [\\\"003\\\"]\\n    \\n  - date: \\\"1944-06-18\\\"\\n    date_precision: \\\"approximate\\\"\\n    event: \\\"Landed Normandy beaches, D+12-14\\\"\\n    confidence: \\\"approximate\\\"\\n    response_ids: [\\\"012\\\"]\\n    note: \\\"Veteran says 'about 12 or 14 days after D-Day'\\\"\\n\\n  - date: \\\"1944-10-08\\\"\\n    date_precision: \\\"day\\\"\\n    event: \\\"Bronze Star action\\\"\\n    confidence: \\\"stated\\\"\\n    response_ids: [\\\"019\\\"]\\n\\n  # ... more events\\n\\nrelationships:\\n  - id: \\\"tipton\\\"\\n    names: [\\\"Tip\\\", \\\"Tipton\\\"]  # All variants found\\n    canonical: \\\"Tipton\\\"\\n    role: \\\"Sergeant in his unit\\\"\\n    context: \\\"Close comrade, present during German tank looting incident\\\"\\n    response_ids: [\\\"028\\\", \\\"029\\\"]\\n    linked_veteran: null  # Could link to another veteran_id if discovered\\n\\n  - id: \\\"monk\\\"\\n    names: [\\\"Monk\\\"]\\n    canonical: \\\"Monk\\\"\\n    role: \\\"Fellow soldier\\\"\\n    context: \\\"Present during German tank looting incident\\\"\\n    response_ids: [\\\"029\\\"]\\n    linked_veteran: null\\n\\n# LLM-identified notable stories\\nnotable_stories:\\n  - id: \\\"german_tank_looting\\\"\\n    title: \\\"Looting the German tank under fire\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Hugo and Tip investigate knocked-out German tank, get ambushed by machine gun, escape on TD\\\"\\n    response_ids: [\\\"029\\\"]\\n    writing_potential: \\\"high\\\"\\n    writing_note: \\\"Action sequence with named characters, tension, escape\\\"\\n\\n  - id: \\\"strawberry_warehouse\\\"\\n    title: \\\"Strawberries in the German warehouse\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"After months of C-rations, finding canned strawberries in captured warehouse\\\"\\n    response_ids: [\\\"014\\\"]\\n    writing_potential: \\\"high\\\"\\n    writing_note: \\\"Humanizing detail, sensory, contrast of war and small pleasures\\\"\\n\\n  - id: \\\"three_minute_shower\\\"\\n    title: \\\"Three-minute shower after five months\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"First shower and clean clothes after five months of continuous combat\\\"\\n    response_ids: [\\\"014\\\"]\\n    writing_potential: \\\"high\\\"\\n    writing_note: \\\"Visceral detail, could open or close a chapter\\\"\\n\\n# LLM-flagged items needing verification\\nverification_needed:\\n  - issue: \\\"Landing date ambiguity\\\"\\n    detail: \\\"Says 'about 12 or 14 days' after D-Day\\\"\\n    response_ids: [\\\"012\\\"]\\n\\n# Source information\\nsource:\\n  file: \\\"girusi_hugo_2005_warhawk.txt\\\"\\n  date_recorded: \\\"2005-05-06\\\"\\n  location: \\\"Warhawk Air Museum, Nampa, Idaho\\\"\\n  interviewer: \\\"James Turner\\\"\\n  project: \\\"Veterans History Project / Library of Congress\\\"\\n\\n# The transcript itself\\nresponses:\\n  - id: \\\"001\\\"\\n    interviewer: \\\"Please give us your full name, address, and birth date...\\\"\\n    veteran: \\\"Well, my name is Hugo Girusi. I'm from Montana...\\\"\\n    \\n    # LLM-extracted metadata for this response\\n    extracted:\\n      summary: \\\"Basic biographical info - name, age (89), from Montana, served in 15th Infantry then 603rd TD Battalion\\\"\\n      dates:\\n        - value: \\\"89 years old\\\"\\n          context: \\\"current age at interview\\\"\\n          precision: \\\"stated\\\"\\n      locations:\\n        - \\\"Montana\\\"\\n        - \\\"Lewiston, Idaho\\\"\\n      people: []\\n      units:\\n        - \\\"15th Infantry\\\"\\n        - \\\"603rd Tank Destroyer Battalion\\\"\\n      topics: [\\\"biographical\\\", \\\"service-overview\\\"]\\n      writing_potential: \\\"low\\\"\\n      writing_note: null\\n\\n    # Paragraphs for search (just the splits, embeddings in SQLite)\\n    paragraphs:\\n      - id: \\\"001_p1\\\"\\n        text: \\\"Well, my name is Hugo Girusi. I'm from Montana...\\\"\\n      - id: \\\"001_p2\\\"\\n        text: \\\"I was in the 15th Infantry for about a year...\\\"\\n\\n  - id: \\\"002\\\"\\n    interviewer: \\\"Explain if you wouldn't mind your time in Montana before the war...\\\"\\n    veteran: \\\"Well, Red Lodge was a mining town and it was a coal mine...\\\"\\n    extracted:\\n      summary: \\\"Pre-war Montana - Red Lodge mining town, mine closed in late 30s, economic hardship, people left for California\\\"\\n      dates:\\n        - value: \\\"late 1930s\\\"\\n          context: \\\"when mine shut down\\\"\\n          precision: \\\"approximate\\\"\\n      locations:\\n        - \\\"Red Lodge, Montana\\\"\\n        - \\\"California\\\"\\n      people: []\\n      units: []\\n      topics: [\\\"pre-war\\\", \\\"hometown\\\", \\\"economic-hardship\\\"]\\n      writing_potential: \\\"medium\\\"\\n      writing_note: \\\"Sets up why he enlisted - no work\\\"\\n    paragraphs:\\n      - id: \\\"002_p1\\\"\\n        text: \\\"Well, Red Lodge was a mining town...\\\"\\n\\n  # ... remaining responses (typically 40-60 per transcript)\\n```\\n\\n### 3.2 Annotations File (`annotations/{veteran_id}.yaml`)\\n\\n```yaml\\n# annotations/girusi_hugo.yaml\\n\\nveteran_id: girusi_hugo\\n\\nresponse_annotations:\\n  \\\"014\\\":\\n    chapter: 4\\n    notes:\\n      - date: \\\"2024-01-15\\\"\\n        text: \\\"Use strawberry story for chapter opening\\\"\\n      - date: \\\"2024-01-20\\\"\\n        text: \\\"Pairs well with Smith's comment about K-rations\\\"\\n    flags: []\\n\\n  \\\"029\\\":\\n    chapter: 5\\n    notes:\\n      - date: \\\"2024-01-16\\\"\\n        text: \\\"Best action sequence - Tip, Monk, machine gun, escape\\\"\\n    flags:\\n      - \\\"needs-map-reference\\\"\\n\\nveteran_notes:\\n  - date: \\\"2024-01-15\\\"\\n    text: \\\"Introduce Hugo in chapter 2, he becomes a recurring voice\\\"\\n  - date: \\\"2024-01-18\\\"\\n    text: \\\"His arc: Montana poverty \\u2192 training \\u2192 combat \\u2192 survival \\u2192 home\\\"\\n\\nresearch_todos:\\n  - \\\"Verify 603rd TD Battalion movements against unit history\\\"\\n  - \\\"Find Tipton in other transcripts or unit roster\\\"\\n  - \\\"Get photo of M-16 tank destroyer for reference\\\"\\n```\\n\\n### 3.3 Config File (`config.yaml`)\\n\\n```yaml\\n# config.yaml\\n\\nllm:\\n  provider: \\\"anthropic\\\"  # anthropic | openai | ollama\\n  model: \\\"claude-sonnet-4-20250514\\\"\\n  api_key_env: \\\"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\\\"  # Environment variable name\\n\\nembeddings:\\n  provider: \\\"openai\\\"  # openai | ollama\\n  model: \\\"text-embedding-3-small\\\"\\n  api_key_env: \\\"OPENAI_API_KEY\\\"\\n\\nchunking:\\n  # How to split responses into paragraphs\\n  method: \\\"double_newline\\\"  # or \\\"sentence_count\\\" or \\\"token_limit\\\"\\n  min_paragraph_length: 50  # characters, don't create tiny paragraphs\\n\\nsearch:\\n  default_limit: 20\\n  hybrid_weight: 0.7  # 0 = keyword only, 1 = semantic only\\n\\nexport:\\n  default_format: \\\"markdown\\\"\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. CLI Interface\\n\\n### 4.1 Ingestion\\n\\n```bash\\n# Ingest a new transcript\\noralhistory ingest <transcript_file> --veteran \\\"Hugo Girusi\\\"\\n\\n# Options:\\n#   --veteran    Veteran's full name (required)\\n#   --unit       Military unit (optional, LLM will try to extract)\\n#   --source     Source description (optional)\\n#   --dry-run    Show what would be extracted without saving\\n\\n# Example:\\noralhistory ingest transcripts/girusi_2005.txt --veteran \\\"Hugo Girusi\\\"\\n\\n# Output:\\n# Parsing transcript... 47 responses found\\n# Extracting metadata... [\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588] 47/47\\n# Synthesizing veteran profile...\\n# Building timeline... 23 events\\n# Identifying relationships... 8 people\\n# Finding notable stories... 5 high-potential\\n# Generating embeddings... [\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588] 152 paragraphs\\n# \\n# \\u2713 Saved: veterans/girusi_hugo.yaml\\n# \\u2713 Indexed: 47 responses, 152 paragraphs\\n#\\n# Verification needed:\\n#   - Landing date ambiguity (D+12 vs D+14)\\n#\\n# Notable stories found:\\n#   - \\\"Looting the German tank under fire\\\" (HIGH)\\n#   - \\\"Strawberries in the German warehouse\\\" (HIGH)\\n#   - \\\"Three-minute shower after five months\\\" (HIGH)\\n```\\n\\n### 4.2 Search\\n\\n```bash\\n# Semantic search across all veterans\\noralhistory search <query>\\n\\n# Options:\\n#   --limit      Max results (default: 20)\\n#   --veteran    Filter to specific veteran\\n#   --chapter    Filter to responses assigned to chapter\\n#   --topic      Filter by extracted topic\\n#   --potential  Filter by writing potential (low/medium/high)\\n\\n# Examples:\\noralhistory search \\\"tank destroyer training\\\"\\noralhistory search \\\"food rations hardship\\\"\\noralhistory search \\\"scared first combat\\\" --potential high\\noralhistory search \\\"Camp Hood\\\" --veteran \\\"Hugo Girusi\\\"\\n\\n# Output:\\n# \\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\n# SEARCH: \\\"food rations hardship\\\" (3 veterans, 5 responses)\\n# \\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\n#\\n# \\u250c\\u2500 HUGO GIRUSI \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n# \\u2502  603rd Tank Destroyer Battalion | Staff Sergeant\\n# \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n# \\u2502\\n# \\u2502  [014] \\u2605 HIGH POTENTIAL\\n# \\u2502  Topic: Poor nutrition, looting warehouses\\n# \\u2502  LLM: \\\"Vivid detail about strawberries - humanizing moment\\\"\\n# \\u2502  Chapter: 4\\n# \\u2502\\n# \\u2502  Q: What was your life like during September, October,\\n# \\u2502     November of '44?\\n# \\u2502\\n# \\u2502  \\\"...we ate C-rations for five months. And we never had a\\n# \\u2502   change of clothes for five months... every once in a while\\n# \\u2502   we'd break into some German warehouse and we'd find cans\\n# \\u2502   of food to eat... I remember one warehouse we found can\\n# \\u2502   after can of strawberries, and we ate strawberries until\\n# \\u2502   we couldn't eat them anymore.\\\"\\n# \\u2502\\n# \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n#\\n# \\u250c\\u2500 JOHN SMITH \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n# \\u2502  6th Armored Division | Corporal\\n# \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n# \\u2502  ...\\n```\\n\\n### 4.3 Veteran Commands\\n\\n```bash\\n# List all veterans\\noralhistory veterans\\n\\n# Output:\\n# VETERANS (4 total)\\n# \\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\n# girusi_hugo      Hugo Girusi       603rd TD Battalion    47 responses\\n# smith_john       John Smith        6th Armored, B Co     62 responses\\n# ...\\n\\n# Show veteran profile\\noralhistory veteran <veteran_id>\\noralhistory veteran girusi_hugo\\n\\n# Output:\\n# \\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\n# HUGO GIRUSI\\n# \\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\n# Unit:     603rd Tank Destroyer Battalion\\n# Rank:     Staff Sergeant\\n# Service:  1941 - 1945\\n# Source:   girusi_hugo_2005_warhawk.txt (2005-05-06)\\n#\\n# TIMELINE (23 events)\\n# \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n# 1941          Enlisted at Fort Lewis [003]\\n# 1941-1942     15th Infantry, Fort Lewis [004]\\n# 1942-1944     Various training locations [007, 008]\\n# 1944-06 (~)   Landed Normandy, D+12-14 [012] \\u26a0 verify\\n# ...\\n#\\n# RELATIONSHIPS (8 people)\\n# \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n# Tipton        Sergeant, close comrade [028, 029]\\n# Monk          Fellow soldier [029]\\n# ...\\n#\\n# NOTABLE STORIES (5)\\n# \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n# \\u2605 Looting the German tank under fire [029]\\n# \\u2605 Strawberries in the German warehouse [014]\\n# \\u2605 Three-minute shower after five months [014]\\n# ...\\n#\\n# VERIFICATION NEEDED\\n# \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n# \\u26a0 Landing date ambiguity (D+12 vs D+14) [012]\\n\\n# Show timeline only\\noralhistory veteran girusi_hugo --timeline\\n\\n# Show relationships only\\noralhistory veteran girusi_hugo --relationships\\n\\n# Show all responses (full transcript)\\noralhistory veteran girusi_hugo --responses\\n\\n# Show specific response\\noralhistory veteran girusi_hugo --response 014\\n```\\n\\n### 4.4 Annotations\\n\\n```bash\\n# Add a note to a response\\noralhistory annotate <veteran_id> <response_id> --note \\\"Your note here\\\"\\noralhistory annotate girusi_hugo 014 --note \\\"Use for chapter opening\\\"\\n\\n# Assign to chapter\\noralhistory annotate girusi_hugo 014 --chapter 4\\n\\n# Add flag\\noralhistory annotate girusi_hugo 029 --flag \\\"needs-map-reference\\\"\\n\\n# Remove flag\\noralhistory annotate girusi_hugo 029 --remove-flag \\\"needs-map-reference\\\"\\n\\n# Add note to veteran (not specific response)\\noralhistory annotate girusi_hugo --veteran-note \\\"Introduce in chapter 2\\\"\\n\\n# Add research todo\\noralhistory annotate girusi_hugo --todo \\\"Verify unit movements against history\\\"\\n\\n# View all annotations for a veteran\\noralhistory annotations girusi_hugo\\n\\n# View all annotations for a chapter\\noralhistory annotations --chapter 4\\n\\n# View all flags\\noralhistory annotations --flags\\n```\\n\\n### 4.5 Connections (Cross-Veteran)\\n\\n```bash\\n# Find potential connections across veterans\\noralhistory connections\\n\\n# Output:\\n# POTENTIAL CONNECTIONS\\n# \\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\n#\\n# PERSON: \\\"Tipton\\\" / \\\"Sergeant Tipton\\\"\\n# \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n# girusi_hugo: \\\"Tip\\\", \\\"Tipton\\\" - Sergeant, close comrade\\n# smith_john:  \\\"Sergeant Tipton\\\" - Training instructor at Camp Hood\\n# \\u2192 Possible same person. Confirm?\\n#\\n# UNIT: \\\"6th Armored Division\\\"\\n# \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n# girusi_hugo: Attached to 6th Armored (603rd TD)\\n# smith_john:  Served in 6th Armored, Company B\\n# jones_will:  Served in 6th Armored, HQ Company\\n# \\u2192 Same unit, likely knew each other or shared experiences\\n\\n# Confirm a connection\\noralhistory connect girusi_hugo:tipton smith_john:sergeant_tipton\\n\\n# Output:\\n# \\u2713 Linked: girusi_hugo:tipton \\u2194 smith_john:sergeant_tipton\\n# Both now reference each other in relationship data.\\n\\n# Search for a specific person across all veterans\\noralhistory connections --search \\\"Tipton\\\"\\n```\\n\\n### 4.6 Chapter Management\\n\\n```bash\\n# Show all responses assigned to a chapter\\noralhistory chapter <number>\\noralhistory chapter 4\\n\\n# Output:\\n# \\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\n# CHAPTER 4 (12 responses from 4 veterans)\\n# \\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\n#\\n# HUGO GIRUSI (3 responses)\\n# \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n# [014] \\u2605 \\\"Strawberries in the warehouse\\\"\\n#       Note: \\\"Use for chapter opening\\\"\\n#\\n# [015] \\\"Daily routine in a TD battalion\\\"\\n#\\n# [016] \\\"Vehicle maintenance and fuel consumption\\\"\\n#\\n# JOHN SMITH (4 responses)\\n# \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n# ...\\n\\n# Export chapter for writing\\noralhistory chapter 4 --export\\n\\n# Output:\\n# \\u2713 Exported: exports/chapter_04.md\\n```\\n\\n### 4.7 Export\\n\\n```bash\\n# Export a chapter\\noralhistory export chapter <number>\\noralhistory export chapter 4\\n\\n# Export a veteran's full material\\noralhistory export veteran <veteran_id>\\noralhistory export veteran girusi_hugo\\n\\n# Export search results\\noralhistory search \\\"Brittany campaign\\\" --export brittany_material\\n\\n# Export all notable stories\\noralhistory export stories\\n\\n# Export timeline across all veterans\\noralhistory export timeline --start 1944-06 --end 1944-09\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Export Format\\n\\n### 5.1 Chapter Export (`exports/chapter_04.md`)\\n\\n```markdown\\n# Chapter 4 - Research Material\\n\\n> Generated: 2024-01-20\\n> Responses: 12 from 4 veterans\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Hugo Girusi\\n**603rd Tank Destroyer Battalion | Staff Sergeant**\\n\\n### [014] Poor nutrition and warehouse looting \\u2605\\n\\n**Writing potential:** HIGH\\n**LLM note:** Vivid detail about strawberries - humanizing moment\\n**Your notes:**\\n- Use for chapter opening\\n- Pairs well with Smith's comment about K-rations\\n\\n**Q:** What was your life like during September, October, November of '44?\\n\\n> Well, I'm glad you asked that, because we were on a -- we were detached to -- and so we ate C-rations for five months. And we never had a change of clothes for five months. And that's clear up until the following year. And when we got a change of clothes, we were able to take a shower. And I still remember that the man that gave us a shower said, \\\"You've got three minutes.\\\" Did you ever try to take a shower in three minutes? Wow. I'll tell you, you step it up right quick-like. But anyway, you get clean. And we lost -- everybody in our company lost pound after pound because the C-rations weren't doing too good for us. But we kept alive, and every once in a while we'd break into some German warehouse and we'd find cans of food to eat, and we'd eat. I remember one warehouse we found can after can of strawberries, and we ate strawberries until we couldn't eat them anymore. In another one we ate ham. We had ham after ham. But they helped us out.\\n\\n**Extracted:**\\n- Topics: daily life, food/rations, hardship\\n- Dates: 5 months (duration of hardship)\\n- Locations: German warehouse (unspecified)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### [015] Daily routine in a TD battalion\\n\\n...\\n\\n---\\n\\n## John Smith\\n**6th Armored Division, Company B | Corporal**\\n\\n...\\n```\\n\\n### 5.2 Veteran Export (`exports/veteran_girusi_hugo.md`)\\n\\n```markdown\\n# Hugo Girusi - Complete Research Material\\n\\n> Generated: 2024-01-20\\n> Source: girusi_hugo_2005_warhawk.txt\\n> Recorded: 2005-05-06 at Warhawk Air Museum\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Profile\\n\\n- **Unit:** 603rd Tank Destroyer Battalion\\n- **Rank:** Staff Sergeant\\n- **Service:** 1941 - 1945\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline\\n\\n| Date | Event | Confidence | Response |\\n|------|-------|------------|----------|\\n| 1941 | Enlisted at Fort Lewis | inferred | [003] |\\n| 1941-1942 | 15th Infantry, Fort Lewis | stated | [004] |\\n| 1944-06 (~) | Landed Normandy, D+12-14 | approximate \\u26a0 | [012] |\\n| 1944-10-08 | Bronze Star action | stated | [019] |\\n| ... | ... | ... | ... |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Relationships\\n\\n### Tipton (Sergeant)\\n- **Also known as:** Tip\\n- **Context:** Close comrade, present during German tank looting incident\\n- **Responses:** [028], [029]\\n\\n### Monk (Fellow soldier)\\n- **Context:** Present during German tank looting incident\\n- **Responses:** [029]\\n\\n...\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Notable Stories\\n\\n### \\u2605 Looting the German tank under fire\\n**Response:** [029]\\n**Writing note:** Action sequence with named characters, tension, escape\\n\\n> Tipton and I\\u2014Tip was a sergeant of mine\\u2014we decided to go investigate a German tank that had been knocked out. So we got on our TD and took off for the tank, and we thought we'd get looted. Well, we got there, and I sent the TD back to the bunch. And just as we started looting that tank, a squarehead out there got up and sprayed us with a machine gun...\\n\\n---\\n\\n## All Responses\\n\\n### [001] Basic biographical information\\n...\\n\\n### [002] Pre-war Montana\\n...\\n\\n(continues with all 47 responses)\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. LLM Prompts\\n\\n### 6.1 Response Extraction Prompt\\n\\n```\\nYou are analyzing a WWII oral history interview response. Extract structured metadata.\\n\\nINTERVIEWER: {interviewer_question}\\nVETERAN: {veteran_response}\\n\\nExtract the following as JSON:\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"One sentence summary of what the veteran discusses\\\",\\n  \\\"dates\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"value\\\": \\\"The date or time period mentioned\\\",\\n      \\\"context\\\": \\\"What this date refers to\\\",\\n      \\\"precision\\\": \\\"stated | inferred | approximate\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"locations\\\": [\\\"List of geographic locations mentioned\\\"],\\n  \\\"people\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Name or nickname as stated\\\",\\n      \\\"role\\\": \\\"Their role if clear (sergeant, friend, officer, etc.)\\\",\\n      \\\"context\\\": \\\"Brief context of how they're mentioned\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"units\\\": [\\\"Military units mentioned\\\"],\\n  \\\"events\\\": [\\\"Specific events or incidents described\\\"],\\n  \\\"topics\\\": [\\\"Relevant topics from: combat, training, daily-life, hardship, humor, loss, equipment, medical, prisoners, civilians, leadership, fear, friendship, home-front, post-war\\\"],\\n  \\\"writing_potential\\\": \\\"low | medium | high\\\",\\n  \\\"writing_note\\\": \\\"If medium or high potential, explain why this is valuable for a book (vivid detail, unique perspective, emotional resonance, action, humor, etc.). null if low potential.\\\"\\n}\\n\\nGuidelines:\\n- For dates, distinguish between explicitly stated (\\\"October 8, 1944\\\") and inferred/approximate (\\\"about a year before Pearl Harbor\\\")\\n- For people, capture all name variants (e.g., \\\"Tip\\\" and \\\"Tipton\\\" for same person)\\n- writing_potential is HIGH if: vivid sensory detail, strong narrative moment, emotional resonance, unique perspective, humor, action sequence\\n- writing_potential is MEDIUM if: useful context, fills gaps, corroborates other accounts\\n- writing_potential is LOW if: routine biographical info, vague recollections, administrative details\\n```\\n\\n### 6.2 Veteran Synthesis Prompt\\n\\n```\\nYou are synthesizing a WWII veteran's complete oral history interview for book research.\\n\\nVeteran: {veteran_name}\\nNumber of responses: {count}\\n\\nHere are all the extracted response metadata:\\n\\n{all_response_extractions_as_json}\\n\\nSynthesize the following:\\n\\n## 1. Timeline\\nCreate a chronological timeline of events from the veteran's service. Include:\\n- date (as specific as possible, or approximate)\\n- date_precision: \\\"year\\\" | \\\"month\\\" | \\\"day\\\" | \\\"approximate\\\"\\n- event description\\n- confidence: \\\"stated\\\" (veteran explicitly said this date) | \\\"inferred\\\" (derived from context) | \\\"approximate\\\" (veteran used vague terms like \\\"about\\\" or \\\"around\\\")\\n- response_ids that support this event\\n- note (if there's ambiguity or need for verification)\\n\\n## 2. Relationships\\nIdentify all people mentioned by the veteran:\\n- Consolidate name variants (e.g., \\\"Tip\\\" and \\\"Tipton\\\" are likely the same person)\\n- canonical name (best/most complete version)\\n- all name variants found\\n- role (if determinable)\\n- context (how they relate to the veteran)\\n- response_ids where they appear\\n\\n## 3. Notable Stories\\nIdentify the top stories that would be most valuable for a book:\\n- title (short, descriptive)\\n- summary (2-3 sentences)\\n- response_ids\\n- writing_potential (should all be \\\"high\\\")\\n- writing_note (why this story matters - drama, humor, humanity, unique detail)\\n\\nLook for:\\n- Action sequences with tension\\n- Moments of humanity amid war\\n- Vivid sensory details\\n- Humor or irony\\n- Emotional turning points\\n- Unique perspectives not commonly recorded\\n\\n## 4. Verification Needed\\nFlag anything that seems ambiguous, contradictory, or would benefit from external verification:\\n- issue description\\n- detail\\n- response_ids\\n\\nReturn as JSON matching this structure:\\n{\\n  \\\"timeline\\\": [...],\\n  \\\"relationships\\\": [...],\\n  \\\"notable_stories\\\": [...],\\n  \\\"verification_needed\\\": [...]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### 6.3 Relationship Deduplication Prompt (Within Veteran)\\n\\n```\\nThese names were extracted from a single veteran's oral history. Identify which names likely refer to the same person.\\n\\nNames found:\\n{list_of_all_names_with_context}\\n\\nFor each unique person, return:\\n{\\n  \\\"canonical\\\": \\\"Most complete/formal version of the name\\\",\\n  \\\"variants\\\": [\\\"All versions found in transcript\\\"],\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"certain | likely | possible\\\",\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Why you believe these are the same person\\\"\\n}\\n\\nOnly group names if there's reasonable evidence they're the same person (same role, similar context, nickname patterns like \\\"Tip/Tipton\\\").\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Technical Implementation\\n\\n### 7.1 Technology Stack\\n\\n- **Language:** Python 3.11+\\n- **CLI Framework:** Click\\n- **LLM:** Anthropic Claude (configurable)\\n- **Embeddings:** OpenAI text-embedding-3-small (configurable)\\n- **Vector Search:** SQLite + sqlite-vss\\n- **Data Storage:** YAML (veterans, annotations) + SQLite (indexes)\\n- **Version Control:** Git (user's responsibility to init/commit)\\n\\n### 7.2 Dependencies\\n\\n```\\n# requirements.txt\\nclick>=8.0\\npyyaml>=6.0\\nanthropic>=0.18\\nopenai>=1.0\\nsqlite-vss>=0.1.2\\nnumpy>=1.24\\nrich>=13.0        # Pretty terminal output\\n```\\n\\n### 7.3 Project Structure\\n\\n```\\noralhistory/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 __init__.py\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 cli.py              # Click CLI definition\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 models.py           # Pydantic models for Veteran, Response, etc.\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 storage.py          # YAML read/write, file management\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 parser.py           # Transcript parsing (Q&A splitting)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 search.py           # Vector search, hybrid search\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 export.py           # Markdown export generation\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 llm/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 __init__.py\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 client.py       # LLM client abstraction\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 extractor.py    # Response extraction\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 synthesizer.py  # Veteran profile synthesis\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 tests/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ...\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 config.yaml\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 requirements.txt\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 setup.py\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 README.md\\n```\\n\\n### 7.4 Embedding Strategy\\n\\n**What gets embedded:**\\n1. Each paragraph (for precision search)\\n2. Each full response with interviewer question prepended (for context)\\n\\n**Embedding text format:**\\n```\\n[Paragraph]\\n\\\"The barracks were these tar paper shacks, cold as hell at night, hot during the day. Sand everywhere.\\\"\\n\\n[Full Response]\\n\\\"Q: What do you remember about arriving at Camp Cooke? A: Oh god, that place. We pulled in on these cattle cars...\\\"\\n```\\n\\n**Hybrid search:**\\n1. Embed query\\n2. Search paragraphs by cosine similarity\\n3. Also do keyword search on full response text\\n4. Combine results (configurable weighting)\\n5. Group by veteran, return full responses\\n\\n### 7.5 Transcript Parsing Rules\\n\\nFor interview-format transcripts:\\n\\n1. **Detect speaker pattern:** Look for consistent patterns like:\\n   - `INTERVIEWER:` / `VETERAN:`\\n   - `Q:` / `A:`\\n   - Speaker names followed by colons\\n   \\n2. **Split on interviewer turns:** Each interviewer utterance starts a new response\\n\\n3. **Handle edge cases:**\\n   - Interviewer follow-ups mid-response \\u2192 keep with previous response\\n   - Very short veteran answers \\u2192 still separate response\\n   - Stage directions or notes in brackets \\u2192 preserve but don't embed\\n\\n4. **Paragraph splitting within responses:**\\n   - Split on double newlines\\n   - Or split on significant pause indicators\\n   - Minimum paragraph length: 50 characters\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Workflow Summary\\n\\n### 8.1 Initial Setup\\n\\n```bash\\n# Create project directory\\nmkdir my_book_research\\ncd my_book_research\\n\\n# Initialize\\noralhistory init\\n\\n# Configure LLM keys\\nexport ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=\\\"...\\\"\\nexport OPENAI_API_KEY=\\\"...\\\"\\n\\n# Initialize git (recommended)\\ngit init\\n```\\n\\n### 8.2 Adding Transcripts\\n\\n```bash\\n# Add each transcript\\noralhistory ingest transcripts/girusi_2005.txt --veteran \\\"Hugo Girusi\\\"\\noralhistory ingest transcripts/smith_2003.txt --veteran \\\"John Smith\\\"\\n\\n# Review what was extracted\\noralhistory veteran girusi_hugo\\noralhistory veteran smith_john\\n\\n# Commit\\ngit add .\\ngit commit -m \\\"Added Girusi and Smith transcripts\\\"\\n```\\n\\n### 8.3 Research Phase\\n\\n```bash\\n# Explore by topic\\noralhistory search \\\"tank destroyer training\\\"\\noralhistory search \\\"first combat\\\"\\noralhistory search \\\"Battle of the Bulge cold weather\\\"\\n\\n# Explore by veteran\\noralhistory veteran girusi_hugo --timeline\\noralhistory veteran girusi_hugo --responses\\n\\n# Find connections\\noralhistory connections\\noralhistory connect girusi_hugo:tipton smith_john:sergeant_tipton\\n```\\n\\n### 8.4 Writing Preparation\\n\\n```bash\\n# Assign to chapters as you find material\\noralhistory annotate girusi_hugo 014 --chapter 4 --note \\\"Opening anecdote\\\"\\noralhistory annotate smith_john 023 --chapter 4 --note \\\"Contrasting perspective\\\"\\n\\n# Review chapter material\\noralhistory chapter 4\\n\\n# Export for writing\\noralhistory chapter 4 --export\\n\\n# Write!\\n```\\n\\n### 8.5 Ongoing\\n\\n```bash\\n# Add more transcripts as you get them\\noralhistory ingest transcripts/jones_2010.txt --veteran \\\"William Jones\\\"\\n\\n# Search across growing collection\\noralhistory search \\\"Brest siege\\\"\\n\\n# Keep annotating\\noralhistory annotate jones_william 015 --chapter 5\\n\\n# Commit regularly\\ngit add .\\ngit commit -m \\\"Added Jones, assigned to chapter 5\\\"\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Future Expansion (Out of Scope for v1)\\n\\nThese features are explicitly not in v1 but the architecture should not prevent them:\\n\\n- **Additional source types:** Photos, newspaper clippings, unit histories\\n- **Usage tracking:** \\\"This passage was used on page 73\\\"\\n- **Collaboration:** Multi-user access, shared annotations\\n- **Web interface:** GUI alternative to CLI\\n- **Timeline visualization:** Interactive timeline across all veterans\\n- **Map integration:** Geographic visualization of movements\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Success Criteria\\n\\nThe system is successful if:\\n\\n1. **Ingesting a transcript takes < 5 minutes** (including LLM processing)\\n2. **Searching returns relevant results** that a human would also find relevant\\n3. **Veterans stay connected to their words** - no orphaned passages\\n4. **The writer can prepare a chapter** by searching, collecting, and exporting in under 30 minutes\\n5. **Nothing is lost** - git history preserves all changes\\n6. **It stays out of the way** - the tool serves the writing, not the other way around\\n\\n---\\n\\n*Document version: 1.0*\\n\",\"file_size_bytes\":33124,\"content_length\":30104}"}],"structuredContent":{"result":"{\"success\":true,\"file_path\":\"/Users/happyhawking/Documents/Projects/Current/writer/specs.md\",\"content\":\"# Oral History Book Research System\\n\\n## Specification Document v1.0\\n\\nA CLI tool for managing WWII oral history transcripts, designed for book research. Veterans are first-class citizens - every search, every passage, every insight stays connected to the person who lived it.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Core Concepts\\n\\n### 1.1 The Veteran (Primary Entity)\\n\\nThe veteran is the central organizing principle. They are characters in your book, not just metadata on a transcript.\\n\\n```\\nVETERAN\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 identity (name, unit, rank, service dates)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 timeline (events, ordered chronologically)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 relationships (people they mention)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 transcript (Q&A responses)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 responses[]\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 text (interviewer question + veteran answer)\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 extracted metadata (LLM-generated)\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 paragraphs[] (for precise search)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 notes (your writer annotations)\\n```\\n\\n### 1.2 The Response (Atomic Unit of Testimony)\\n\\nA response is one interviewer question paired with the veteran's complete answer. This is the natural unit of oral history - one topic, one narrative block.\\n\\nResponses are never split arbitrarily. They may contain multiple paragraphs (for search precision), but retrieval always returns the full response.\\n\\n### 1.3 The Paragraph (Search Precision Layer)\\n\\nParagraphs exist only for embedding/search. When a search hits a paragraph, the system returns its parent response. You never see orphaned paragraphs.\\n\\n### 1.4 Annotations (Your Writer's Layer)\\n\\nAnnotations are your notes, chapter assignments, and flags. They attach to responses but live separately - source material is immutable, your interpretation is mutable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. File Structure\\n\\n```\\noralhistory/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 .git/                          # Version control\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 config.yaml                    # System configuration\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 veterans/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 {veteran_id}.yaml          # One file per veteran (profile + transcript)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 annotations/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 {veteran_id}.yaml          # Your notes per veteran\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 index/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 embeddings.sqlite          # Vector search (SQLite + sqlite-vss)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 relationships.sqlite       # Cross-veteran connections\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 exports/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 {export_name}.md           # Generated exports\\n```\\n\\n### 2.1 Why This Structure\\n\\n- **YAML for veterans**: Human-readable, git-diffable, editable by hand if needed\\n- **Separate annotations**: Your work distinct from source material\\n- **SQLite for indexes**: Fast search, embeddings, no external dependencies\\n- **Git-backed**: Every change tracked, undo anything\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Data Models\\n\\n### 3.1 Veteran File (`veterans/{veteran_id}.yaml`)\\n\\n```yaml\\n# veterans/girusi_hugo.yaml\\n\\nid: girusi_hugo\\nname: \\\"Hugo Girusi\\\"\\nunit: \\\"603rd Tank Destroyer Battalion\\\"\\nrank: \\\"Staff Sergeant\\\"\\nservice_dates:\\n  start: \\\"1941\\\"\\n  end: \\\"1945\\\"\\n\\n# LLM-synthesized from transcript\\ntimeline:\\n  - date: \\\"1941\\\"\\n    date_precision: \\\"year\\\"  # year | month | day | approximate\\n    event: \\\"Enlisted at Fort Lewis\\\"\\n    confidence: \\\"inferred\\\"  # stated | inferred | approximate\\n    response_ids: [\\\"003\\\"]\\n    \\n  - date: \\\"1944-06-18\\\"\\n    date_precision: \\\"approximate\\\"\\n    event: \\\"Landed Normandy beaches, D+12-14\\\"\\n    confidence: \\\"approximate\\\"\\n    response_ids: [\\\"012\\\"]\\n    note: \\\"Veteran says 'about 12 or 14 days after D-Day'\\\"\\n\\n  - date: \\\"1944-10-08\\\"\\n    date_precision: \\\"day\\\"\\n    event: \\\"Bronze Star action\\\"\\n    confidence: \\\"stated\\\"\\n    response_ids: [\\\"019\\\"]\\n\\n  # ... more events\\n\\nrelationships:\\n  - id: \\\"tipton\\\"\\n    names: [\\\"Tip\\\", \\\"Tipton\\\"]  # All variants found\\n    canonical: \\\"Tipton\\\"\\n    role: \\\"Sergeant in his unit\\\"\\n    context: \\\"Close comrade, present during German tank looting incident\\\"\\n    response_ids: [\\\"028\\\", \\\"029\\\"]\\n    linked_veteran: null  # Could link to another veteran_id if discovered\\n\\n  - id: \\\"monk\\\"\\n    names: [\\\"Monk\\\"]\\n    canonical: \\\"Monk\\\"\\n    role: \\\"Fellow soldier\\\"\\n    context: \\\"Present during German tank looting incident\\\"\\n    response_ids: [\\\"029\\\"]\\n    linked_veteran: null\\n\\n# LLM-identified notable stories\\nnotable_stories:\\n  - id: \\\"german_tank_looting\\\"\\n    title: \\\"Looting the German tank under fire\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Hugo and Tip investigate knocked-out German tank, get ambushed by machine gun, escape on TD\\\"\\n    response_ids: [\\\"029\\\"]\\n    writing_potential: \\\"high\\\"\\n    writing_note: \\\"Action sequence with named characters, tension, escape\\\"\\n\\n  - id: \\\"strawberry_warehouse\\\"\\n    title: \\\"Strawberries in the German warehouse\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"After months of C-rations, finding canned strawberries in captured warehouse\\\"\\n    response_ids: [\\\"014\\\"]\\n    writing_potential: \\\"high\\\"\\n    writing_note: \\\"Humanizing detail, sensory, contrast of war and small pleasures\\\"\\n\\n  - id: \\\"three_minute_shower\\\"\\n    title: \\\"Three-minute shower after five months\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"First shower and clean clothes after five months of continuous combat\\\"\\n    response_ids: [\\\"014\\\"]\\n    writing_potential: \\\"high\\\"\\n    writing_note: \\\"Visceral detail, could open or close a chapter\\\"\\n\\n# LLM-flagged items needing verification\\nverification_needed:\\n  - issue: \\\"Landing date ambiguity\\\"\\n    detail: \\\"Says 'about 12 or 14 days' after D-Day\\\"\\n    response_ids: [\\\"012\\\"]\\n\\n# Source information\\nsource:\\n  file: \\\"girusi_hugo_2005_warhawk.txt\\\"\\n  date_recorded: \\\"2005-05-06\\\"\\n  location: \\\"Warhawk Air Museum, Nampa, Idaho\\\"\\n  interviewer: \\\"James Turner\\\"\\n  project: \\\"Veterans History Project / Library of Congress\\\"\\n\\n# The transcript itself\\nresponses:\\n  - id: \\\"001\\\"\\n    interviewer: \\\"Please give us your full name, address, and birth date...\\\"\\n    veteran: \\\"Well, my name is Hugo Girusi. I'm from Montana...\\\"\\n    \\n    # LLM-extracted metadata for this response\\n    extracted:\\n      summary: \\\"Basic biographical info - name, age (89), from Montana, served in 15th Infantry then 603rd TD Battalion\\\"\\n      dates:\\n        - value: \\\"89 years old\\\"\\n          context: \\\"current age at interview\\\"\\n          precision: \\\"stated\\\"\\n      locations:\\n        - \\\"Montana\\\"\\n        - \\\"Lewiston, Idaho\\\"\\n      people: []\\n      units:\\n        - \\\"15th Infantry\\\"\\n        - \\\"603rd Tank Destroyer Battalion\\\"\\n      topics: [\\\"biographical\\\", \\\"service-overview\\\"]\\n      writing_potential: \\\"low\\\"\\n      writing_note: null\\n\\n    # Paragraphs for search (just the splits, embeddings in SQLite)\\n    paragraphs:\\n      - id: \\\"001_p1\\\"\\n        text: \\\"Well, my name is Hugo Girusi. I'm from Montana...\\\"\\n      - id: \\\"001_p2\\\"\\n        text: \\\"I was in the 15th Infantry for about a year...\\\"\\n\\n  - id: \\\"002\\\"\\n    interviewer: \\\"Explain if you wouldn't mind your time in Montana before the war...\\\"\\n    veteran: \\\"Well, Red Lodge was a mining town and it was a coal mine...\\\"\\n    extracted:\\n      summary: \\\"Pre-war Montana - Red Lodge mining town, mine closed in late 30s, economic hardship, people left for California\\\"\\n      dates:\\n        - value: \\\"late 1930s\\\"\\n          context: \\\"when mine shut down\\\"\\n          precision: \\\"approximate\\\"\\n      locations:\\n        - \\\"Red Lodge, Montana\\\"\\n        - \\\"California\\\"\\n      people: []\\n      units: []\\n      topics: [\\\"pre-war\\\", \\\"hometown\\\", \\\"economic-hardship\\\"]\\n      writing_potential: \\\"medium\\\"\\n      writing_note: \\\"Sets up why he enlisted - no work\\\"\\n    paragraphs:\\n      - id: \\\"002_p1\\\"\\n        text: \\\"Well, Red Lodge was a mining town...\\\"\\n\\n  # ... remaining responses (typically 40-60 per transcript)\\n```\\n\\n### 3.2 Annotations File (`annotations/{veteran_id}.yaml`)\\n\\n```yaml\\n# annotations/girusi_hugo.yaml\\n\\nveteran_id: girusi_hugo\\n\\nresponse_annotations:\\n  \\\"014\\\":\\n    chapter: 4\\n    notes:\\n      - date: \\\"2024-01-15\\\"\\n        text: \\\"Use strawberry story for chapter opening\\\"\\n      - date: \\\"2024-01-20\\\"\\n        text: \\\"Pairs well with Smith's comment about K-rations\\\"\\n    flags: []\\n\\n  \\\"029\\\":\\n    chapter: 5\\n    notes:\\n      - date: \\\"2024-01-16\\\"\\n        text: \\\"Best action sequence - Tip, Monk, machine gun, escape\\\"\\n    flags:\\n      - \\\"needs-map-reference\\\"\\n\\nveteran_notes:\\n  - date: \\\"2024-01-15\\\"\\n    text: \\\"Introduce Hugo in chapter 2, he becomes a recurring voice\\\"\\n  - date: \\\"2024-01-18\\\"\\n    text: \\\"His arc: Montana poverty \\u2192 training \\u2192 combat \\u2192 survival \\u2192 home\\\"\\n\\nresearch_todos:\\n  - \\\"Verify 603rd TD Battalion movements against unit history\\\"\\n  - \\\"Find Tipton in other transcripts or unit roster\\\"\\n  - \\\"Get photo of M-16 tank destroyer for reference\\\"\\n```\\n\\n### 3.3 Config File (`config.yaml`)\\n\\n```yaml\\n# config.yaml\\n\\nllm:\\n  provider: \\\"anthropic\\\"  # anthropic | openai | ollama\\n  model: \\\"claude-sonnet-4-20250514\\\"\\n  api_key_env: \\\"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\\\"  # Environment variable name\\n\\nembeddings:\\n  provider: \\\"openai\\\"  # openai | ollama\\n  model: \\\"text-embedding-3-small\\\"\\n  api_key_env: \\\"OPENAI_API_KEY\\\"\\n\\nchunking:\\n  # How to split responses into paragraphs\\n  method: \\\"double_newline\\\"  # or \\\"sentence_count\\\" or \\\"token_limit\\\"\\n  min_paragraph_length: 50  # characters, don't create tiny paragraphs\\n\\nsearch:\\n  default_limit: 20\\n  hybrid_weight: 0.7  # 0 = keyword only, 1 = semantic only\\n\\nexport:\\n  default_format: \\\"markdown\\\"\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. CLI Interface\\n\\n### 4.1 Ingestion\\n\\n```bash\\n# Ingest a new transcript\\noralhistory ingest <transcript_file> --veteran \\\"Hugo Girusi\\\"\\n\\n# Options:\\n#   --veteran    Veteran's full name (required)\\n#   --unit       Military unit (optional, LLM will try to extract)\\n#   --source     Source description (optional)\\n#   --dry-run    Show what would be extracted without saving\\n\\n# Example:\\noralhistory ingest transcripts/girusi_2005.txt --veteran \\\"Hugo Girusi\\\"\\n\\n# Output:\\n# Parsing transcript... 47 responses found\\n# Extracting metadata... [\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588] 47/47\\n# Synthesizing veteran profile...\\n# Building timeline... 23 events\\n# Identifying relationships... 8 people\\n# Finding notable stories... 5 high-potential\\n# Generating embeddings... [\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588\\u2588] 152 paragraphs\\n# \\n# \\u2713 Saved: veterans/girusi_hugo.yaml\\n# \\u2713 Indexed: 47 responses, 152 paragraphs\\n#\\n# Verification needed:\\n#   - Landing date ambiguity (D+12 vs D+14)\\n#\\n# Notable stories found:\\n#   - \\\"Looting the German tank under fire\\\" (HIGH)\\n#   - \\\"Strawberries in the German warehouse\\\" (HIGH)\\n#   - \\\"Three-minute shower after five months\\\" (HIGH)\\n```\\n\\n### 4.2 Search\\n\\n```bash\\n# Semantic search across all veterans\\noralhistory search <query>\\n\\n# Options:\\n#   --limit      Max results (default: 20)\\n#   --veteran    Filter to specific veteran\\n#   --chapter    Filter to responses assigned to chapter\\n#   --topic      Filter by extracted topic\\n#   --potential  Filter by writing potential (low/medium/high)\\n\\n# Examples:\\noralhistory search \\\"tank destroyer training\\\"\\noralhistory search \\\"food rations hardship\\\"\\noralhistory search \\\"scared first combat\\\" --potential high\\noralhistory search \\\"Camp Hood\\\" --veteran \\\"Hugo Girusi\\\"\\n\\n# Output:\\n# \\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\n# SEARCH: \\\"food rations hardship\\\" (3 veterans, 5 responses)\\n# \\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\u2550\\n#\\n# \\u250c\\u2500 HUGO GIRUSI \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n# \\u2502  603rd Tank Destroyer Battalion | Staff Sergeant\\n# \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n# \\u2502\\n# \\u2502  [014] \\u2605 HIGH POTENTIAL\\n# \\u2502  Topic: Poor nutrition, looting warehouses\\n# \\u2502  LLM: \\\"Vivid detail about strawberries - humanizing moment\\\"\\n# \\u2502  Chapter: 4\\n# \\u2502\\n# \\u2502  Q: What was your life like during September, October,\\n# \\u2502     November of '44?\\n# \\u2502\\n# \\u2502  \\\"...we ate C-rations for five months. And we never had a\\n# \\u2502   change of clothes for five months... every once in a while\\n# \\u2502   we'd break into some German warehouse and we'd find cans\\n# \\u2502   of food to eat... I