2025-12-18T10:40:23.904Z [iterm2] [info] Message from client: {"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"write_file","arguments":{"content":"# Oral History Book Research System\n\nA CLI tool for managing WWII oral history transcripts, designed for book research. Veterans are first-class citizens - every search, every passage, every insight stays connected to the person who lived it.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Veteran-centric organization**: Veterans are characters in your book, not just metadata\n- **LLM-powered extraction**: Automatically extracts dates, people, places, and notable stories\n- **Semantic + keyword search**: Find relevant passages across all testimonies\n- **Timeline synthesis**: Chronological view of events across veterans\n- **Relationship mapping**: Track people mentioned and cross-veteran connections\n- **Writing potential scoring**: Identifies high-value passages for your book\n- **Chapter assignment**: Organize material by book chapter\n- **Markdown export**: Generate research documents for writing\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\n# Clone or copy the project\ncd writer\n\n# Create virtual environment\npython -m venv venv\nsource venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: venv\\Scripts\\activate\n\n# Install dependencies\npip install -r requirements.txt\n\n# Install the CLI\npip install -e .\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\nCreate a `.env` file with your API keys:\n\n```bash\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_key_here\nOPENAI_API_KEY=your_key_here  # For embeddings\n```\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\n# Initialize a new project\noralhistory init my_book_research\ncd my_book_research\n\n# Ingest a transcript\noralhistory ingest transcripts/mitchell_1995.txt --veteran \"James Mitchell\"\n\n# View the veteran profile\noralhistory veteran mitchell_james\n\n# Search across testimonies\noralhistory search \"Battle of the Bulge\"\noralhistory search \"food rations hardship\" --potential high\n\n# Assign to chapters\noralhistory annotate mitchell_james 005 --chapter 3 --note \"Great opening scene\"\n\n# Export for writing\noralhistory export chapter 3\noralhistory export veteran mitchell_james\n```\n\n## CLI Commands\n\n### Project Management\n- `oralhistory init [path]` - Initialize a new project\n- `oralhistory veterans` - List all veterans\n\n### Ingestion\n- `oralhistory ingest <file> --veteran \"Name\"` - Ingest a transcript\n\n### Search & Exploration\n- `oralhistory search <query>` - Search across all testimonies\n- `oralhistory veteran <id>` - Show veteran profile\n- `oralhistory veteran <id> --timeline` - Show timeline\n- `oralhistory veteran <id> --relationships` - Show relationships\n- `oralhistory veteran <id> --response 005` - Show specific response\n- `oralhistory connections` - Find cross-veteran connections\n\n### Annotations\n- `oralhistory annotate <veteran> <response> --note \"...\"` - Add note\n- `oralhistory annotate <veteran> <response> --chapter 5` - Assign to chapter\n- `oralhistory annotate <veteran> <response> --flag \"needs-verification\"` - Add flag\n- `oralhistory annotations <veteran>` - View annotations\n- `oralhistory annotations --chapter 5` - View chapter assignments\n\n### Export\n- `oralhistory chapter <number>` - View chapter material\n- `oralhistory chapter <number> --export` - Export chapter\n- `oralhistory export veteran <id>` - Export veteran\n- `oralhistory export stories` - Export all notable stories\n- `oralhistory export timeline --start 1944-06 --end 1944-12` - Export timeline\n\n## File Structure\n\n```\nmy_book_research/\n├── config.yaml           # Configuration\n├── veterans/             # Veteran YAML files\n│   └── mitchell_james.yaml\n├── annotations/          # Your notes and chapter assignments\n│   └── mitchell_james.yaml\n├── index/               # Search indexes\n│   └── embeddings.sqlite\n└── exports/             # Generated exports\n    └── chapter_03.md\n```\n\n## Writing Potential\n\nThe system scores responses by writing potential:\n\n- **HIGH**: Vivid sensory detail, action sequences, named characters, emotional moments, unique perspectives\n- **MEDIUM**: Useful context, fills gaps, corroborates other accounts\n- **LOW**: Routine biographical info, vague recollections, administrative details\n\nUse `--potential high` in search to find the best material.\n\n## Tips for Book Research\n\n1. **Start broad**: Ingest multiple transcripts before diving deep\n2. **Use notable stories**: The LLM identifies the best narrative moments\n3. **Track connections**: Use `oralhistory connections` to find shared experiences\n4. **Export early, export often**: Generate chapter exports as you assign material\n5. **Use git**: Commit after each session to track your research journey\n\n## License\n\nMIT License\n","file_path":"~/Documents/Projects/Current/writer/README.md"}},"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":27} { metadata: undefined }
