2025-12-20T17:38:04.172Z [iterm2] [info] Message from server: {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":76,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"success\":true,\"file_path\":\"/Users/happyhawking/Documents/Projects/Current/writer/src/llm/synthesizer.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nVeteran profile synthesizer for the Oral History Research System.\\n\\nUses LLM to synthesize a veteran's timeline, relationships, and notable stories\\nfrom all their extracted response metadata.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any, Optional\\nimport json\\n\\nfrom .client import LLMClient\\nfrom ..models import (\\n    Response, Veteran, TimelineEvent, Relationship, \\n    NotableStory, VerificationItem, DatePrecision, Confidence, WritingPotential,\\n    VeteranProfile, ThematicStrength, SearchHit\\n)\\n\\n\\nSYNTHESIS_SYSTEM_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are synthesizing a WWII veteran's complete oral history interview for book research.\\nYour task is to create a comprehensive profile that will help a researcher understand this veteran's story.\\nBe meticulous about dates, names, and connections. Flag anything ambiguous for verification.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nPROFILE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE = \\\"\\\"\\\"Synthesize a high-level researcher's profile for this WWII veteran.\\nAnalyze their entire interview and identify their strongest narrative themes, writing potential, and key entities.\\n\\nVeteran: {veteran_name}\\nSummary of all responses:\\n{extractions_json}\\n\\nCreate a profile with:\\n1. Overview: A 3-4 sentence summary of who they were and their main contribution to the war effort.\\n2. Narrative Style: Describe how they tell their story (e.g., \\\"Emotionally detached but technically precise\\\", \\\"Vivid storyteller with strong sensory details\\\", \\\"Focused on interpersonal relationships\\\").\\n3. Thematic Strengths: Identify 3-5 key themes where this veteran provides high-quality information. For each:\\n   - theme: e.g., \\\"Combat\\\", \\\"Training\\\", \\\"Logistics\\\", \\\"Home Front\\\", \\\"POW Life\\\"\\n   - strength: \\\"high\\\" | \\\"medium\\\" | \\\"low\\\"\\n   - summary: Why is this a strength? What specific types of details do they provide?\\n   - response_ids: Which responses support this theme?\\n4. Key Entities: List the 5-10 most important locations, units, or terms associated with this veteran.\\n5. Writing Advice: Advice to the author on how best to use this veteran's testimony in a book.\\n\\nReturn as JSON:\\n{{\\n  \\\"overview\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n  \\\"narrative_style\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n  \\\"thematic_strengths\\\": [\\n    {{\\n      \\\"theme\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n      \\\"strength\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n      \\\"response_ids\\\": [...]\\n    }}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"key_entities\\\": [...],\\n  \\\"writing_advice\\\": \\\"...\\\"\\n}}\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nTOPIC_SYNTHESIS_SYSTEM_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are a master WWII historian and book researcher.\\nYour task is to synthesize multiple accounts from different veterans into a single, cohesive narrative for a book.\\nHighlight areas of consensus and unique perspectives. Always cite your sources using [VeteranID:ResponseID].\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nTOPIC_SYNTHESIS_PROMPT_TEMPLATE = \\\"\\\"\\\"Synthesize the following accounts regarding the topic: \\\"{query}\\\"\\n\\nAccounts:\\n{accounts_json}\\n\\nCreate a narrative synthesis that:\\n1. Provides a cohesive 3-5 paragraph overview of the topic based on these specific accounts.\\n2. WEAVE IN ORIGINAL PASSAGES: Use direct quotes and specific terminology from the veterans' own words. Instead of saying \\\"He described the cold\\\", say \\\"He described how it was '20 below zero with a foot and a half of snow' [veteran:001]\\\".\\n3. Go beyond high-level summaries; use specific descriptions of equipment, weather, emotions, and vivid sensory details from the accounts.\\n4. Highlights unique details that only one veteran mentioned.\\n5. Notes any contradictions or different perspectives on the same event.\\n6. Uses citations like [jarussi_hugo_victor:012] throughout the text.\\n\\nStructure your response with a clear title and sections.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nSYNTHESIS_PROMPT_TEMPLATE = \\\"\\\"\\\"Synthesize this WWII veteran's interview data into a comprehensive profile.\\n\\nVeteran: {veteran_name}\\nNumber of responses: {response_count}\\n\\nHere is the extracted metadata from each response:\\n\\n{extractions_json}\\n\\nCreate a synthesis with:\\n\\n## 1. Timeline\\nCreate a chronological timeline of events. For each event:\\n- date: as specific as possible, or approximate with ~\\n- date_precision: \\\"year\\\" | \\\"month\\\" | \\\"day\\\" | \\\"approximate\\\"\\n- event: description\\n- confidence: \\\"stated\\\" (veteran explicitly said this) | \\\"inferred\\\" (derived from context) | \\\"approximate\\\" (vague terms)\\n- response_ids: list of response IDs that support this event\\n- note: any ambiguity or need for verification (null if clear)\\n\\n## 2. Relationships\\nIdentify all people mentioned:\\n- Consolidate name variants (e.g., \\\"Tip\\\" and \\\"Tipton\\\" are likely the same person)\\n- id: slug identifier for this person\\n- canonical: best/most complete name version\\n- names: all variants found\\n- role: if determinable\\n- context: how they relate to the veteran\\n- response_ids: where they appear\\n\\n## 3. Notable Stories\\nIdentify the TOP 5-10 stories most valuable for a book:\\n- id: slug identifier\\n- title: short, descriptive title\\n- summary: 2-3 sentence summary\\n- response_ids: which responses contain this story\\n- writing_potential: should all be \\\"high\\\"\\n- writing_note: why this story matters (drama, humor, humanity, unique detail, action, sensory detail)\\n\\nLook for:\\n- Action sequences with tension\\n- Moments of humanity amid war\\n- Vivid sensory details (food, weather, sounds, smells)\\n- Humor or irony\\n- Emotional turning points\\n- Unique perspectives not commonly recorded\\n- Named characters and specific places\\n\\n## 4. Verification Needed\\nFlag anything that:\\n- Has conflicting dates\\n- Is ambiguous about locations or people\\n- Would benefit from cross-referencing with unit histories\\n- The veteran expressed uncertainty about\\n\\nReturn as JSON:\\n{{\\n  \\\"timeline\\\": [...],\\n  \\\"relationships\\\": [...],\\n  \\\"notable_stories\\\": [...],\\n  \\\"verification_needed\\\": [...]\\n}}\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass VeteranSynthesizer:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Synthesizes veteran profiles from response extractions.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    \\n    def __init__(self, client: LLMClient):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Initialize synthesizer.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            client: LLM client to use\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self.client = client\\n    \\n    def _prepare_extractions(self, responses: List[Response]) -> str:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Prepare extractions for LLM prompt.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            responses: Responses with extractions\\n            \\n        Returns:\\n            JSON string of extractions\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        extractions = []\\n        \\n        for r in responses:\\n            if r.extracted:\\n                extractions.append({\\n                    \\\"response_id\\\": r.id,\\n                    \\\"interviewer_question\\\": r.interviewer[:200] + \\\"...\\\" if len(r.interviewer) > 200 else r.interviewer,\\n                    \\\"summary\\\": r.extracted.summary,\\n                    \\\"dates\\\": [{\\\"value\\\": d.value, \\\"context\\\": d.context, \\\"precision\\\": d.precision} for d in r.extracted.dates],\\n                    \\\"locations\\\": r.extracted.locations,\\n                    \\\"people\\\": [{\\\"name\\\": p.name, \\\"role\\\": p.role, \\\"context\\\": p.context} for p in r.extracted.people],\\n                    \\\"units\\\": r.extracted.units,\\n                    \\\"events\\\": r.extracted.events,\\n                    \\\"topics\\\": r.extracted.topics,\\n                    \\\"writing_potential\\\": r.extracted.writing_potential.value,\\n                    \\\"writing_note\\\": r.extracted.writing_note,\\n                })\\n        \\n        return json.dumps(extractions, indent=2)\\n    \\n    def synthesize(self, veteran: Veteran) -> Veteran:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Synthesize timeline, relationships, and stories from responses.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            veteran: Veteran with responses and extractions\\n            \\n        Returns:\\n            Updated veteran with synthesized data\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if not veteran.responses:\\n            return veteran\\n        \\n        extractions_json = self._prepare_extractions(veteran.responses)\\n        \\n        prompt = SYNTHESIS_PROMPT_TEMPLATE.format(\\n            veteran_name=veteran.name,\\n            response_count=len(veteran.responses),\\n            extractions_json=extractions_json\\n        )\\n        \\n        try:\\n            data = self.client.complete_json(\\n                prompt=prompt,\\n                system=SYNTHESIS_SYSTEM_PROMPT,\\n                max_tokens=8192\\n            )\\n            \\n            # Parse timeline\\n            timeline = []\\n            for t in data.get(\\\"timeline\\\", []):\\n                if isinstance(t, dict):\\n                    # Parse date precision\\n                    dp_str = t.get(\\\"date_precision\\\", \\\"approximate\\\")\\n                    try:\\n                        date_precision = DatePrecision(dp_str)\\n                    except ValueError:\\n                        date_precision = DatePrecision.APPROXIMATE\\n                    \\n                    # Parse confidence\\n                    conf_str = t.get(\\\"confidence\\\", \\\"inferred\\\")\\n                    try:\\n                        confidence = Confidence(conf_str)\\n                    except ValueError:\\n                        confidence = Confidence.INFERRED\\n                    \\n                    timeline.append(TimelineEvent(\\n                        date=t.get(\\\"date\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        date_precision=date_precision,\\n                        event=t.get(\\\"event\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        confidence=confidence,\\n                        response_ids=t.get(\\\"response_ids\\\", []),\\n                        note=t.get(\\\"note\\\")\\n                    ))\\n            \\n            # Parse relationships\\n            relationships = []\\n            for r in data.get(\\\"relationships\\\", []):\\n                if isinstance(r, dict):\\n                    relationships.append(Relationship(\\n                        id=r.get(\\\"id\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        names=r.get(\\\"names\\\", [r.get(\\\"canonical\\\", \\\"\\\")]),\\n                        canonical=r.get(\\\"canonical\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        role=r.get(\\\"role\\\"),\\n                        context=r.get(\\\"context\\\"),\\n                        response_ids=r.get(\\\"response_ids\\\", []),\\n                        linked_veteran=r.get(\\\"linked_veteran\\\")\\n                    ))\\n            \\n            # Parse notable stories\\n            notable_stories = []\\n            for s in data.get(\\\"notable_stories\\\", []):\\n                if isinstance(s, dict):\\n                    # Parse writing potential\\n                    wp_str = s.get(\\\"writing_potential\\\", \\\"high\\\")\\n                    try:\\n                        writing_potential = WritingPotential(wp_str)\\n                    except ValueError:\\n                        writing_potential = WritingPotential.HIGH\\n                    \\n                    notable_stories.append(NotableStory(\\n                        id=s.get(\\\"id\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        title=s.get(\\\"title\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        summary=s.get(\\\"summary\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        response_ids=s.get(\\\"response_ids\\\", []),\\n                        writing_potential=writing_potential,\\n                        writing_note=s.get(\\\"writing_note\\\")\\n                    ))\\n            \\n            # Parse verification needed\\n            verification_needed = []\\n            for v in data.get(\\\"verification_needed\\\", []):\\n                if isinstance(v, dict):\\n                    verification_needed.append(VerificationItem(\\n                        issue=v.get(\\\"issue\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        detail=v.get(\\\"detail\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        response_ids=v.get(\\\"response_ids\\\", [])\\n                    ))\\n            \\n            # Update veteran\\n            veteran.timeline = timeline\\n            veteran.relationships = relationships\\n            veteran.notable_stories = notable_stories\\n            veteran.verification_needed = verification_needed\\n            \\n            # Also generate narrative profile\\n            narrative_synth = NarrativeSynthesizer(self.client)\\n            veteran.profile = narrative_synth.synthesize_profile(veteran)\\n            \\n        except (json.JSONDecodeError, KeyError) as e:\\n            # Add error to verification\\n            veteran.verification_needed = [\\n                VerificationItem(\\n                    issue=\\\"Synthesis error\\\",\\n                    detail=f\\\"LLM synthesis failed: {str(e)}\\\",\\n                    response_ids=[]\\n                )\\n            ]\\n        \\n        return veteran\\n    \\n    def extract_basic_info(self, responses: List[Response]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Extract basic veteran info (unit, rank, service dates) from responses.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            responses: Responses with extractions\\n            \\n        Returns:\\n            Dict with unit, rank, service_dates\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        units = set()\\n        ranks = set()\\n        dates = []\\n        \\n        for r in responses:\\n            if r.extracted:\\n                for unit in r.extracted.units:\\n                    units.add(unit)\\n                # Look for rank in topics or summary\\n                if \\\"rank\\\" in (r.extracted.summary or \\\"\\\").lower():\\n                    # Try to extract rank\\n                    pass\\n        \\n        return {\\n            \\\"unit\\\": list(units)[0] if units else None,\\n            \\\"rank\\\": list(ranks)[0] if ranks else None,\\n        }\\n\\n\\nDRAFT_SYSTEM_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are a skilled historical writer helping to create first-draft narrative text from WWII oral history interviews.\\nYour task is to use the actual passages from veterans' accounts to tell the story, converting spoken language to written language while preserving their authentic voice.\\nAlways include inline citations in the format (VeteranName, Response XXX) to attribute quotes and information.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nDRAFT_PROMPT_TEMPLATES = {\\n    \\\"narrative\\\": \\\"\\\"\\\"Write a narrative first-draft about \\\"{topic}\\\" using these oral history accounts.\\n\\nAccounts:\\n{accounts_json}\\n\\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:\\n- USE THE ACTUAL PASSAGES EXTENSIVELY - don't just summarize. Quote liberally from the accounts.\\n- Convert spoken language to written language: fix grammar, remove filler words (\\\"um\\\", \\\"you know\\\"), smooth transitions, but PRESERVE the veteran's authentic voice and specific details.\\n- Weave the passages together to tell the story - use the veterans' own words as the foundation of your narrative.\\n- When a passage needs slight tweaking for written flow, make minimal edits that preserve meaning and voice.\\n\\nWrite in a compelling, human narrative style that:\\n1. Opens with a strong hook using one of the actual passages\\n2. Weaves the veterans' actual words throughout - quote extensively, don't paraphrase\\n3. Uses direct quotes with citations like (Rolfes, Response 014) for verbatim quotes\\n4. For passages you've slightly edited for written flow, use citations like (Rolfes, Response 014, adapted)\\n5. Creates vivid scenes using the sensory details from the actual accounts\\n6. Maintains chronological or thematic flow by connecting the passages\\n7. Ends with reflection or significance using the veterans' own words when possible\\n\\nThe draft should feel like the veterans are telling the story through their own words, with minimal narrative scaffolding.\\n\\nTarget length: decide on a suitable number of words for a polished narrative prose.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"documentary\\\": \\\"\\\"\\\"Write a documentary-style draft about \\\"{topic}\\\" using these oral history accounts.\\n\\nAccounts:\\n{accounts_json}\\n\\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:\\n- USE THE ACTUAL PASSAGES EXTENSIVELY - quote liberally, don't summarize.\\n- Convert spoken language to written language: fix grammar, remove filler words, smooth transitions, but PRESERVE the veteran's authentic voice.\\n- Let the veterans' words tell the story - use extensive direct quotes with minimal editorial commentary.\\n\\nWrite in an objective, journalistic style that:\\n1. Presents facts and testimonies in a balanced way using the actual accounts\\n2. Uses extensive direct quotes with citations like (Rolfes, Response 014)\\n3. For passages slightly edited for written flow, use (Rolfes, Response 014, adapted)\\n4. Provides minimal context between quotes - let the quotes do the work\\n5. Acknowledges different perspectives by showing contrasting quotes\\n6. Lets the veterans' words speak for themselves - quote extensively\\n7. Maintains objectivity while honoring the subjects\\n\\nThe draft should be primarily the veterans' own words with minimal narrative intervention.\\n\\nTarget length: decide on a suitable number of words\\n\\\"\\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"academic\\\": \\\"\\\"\\\"Write an academic-style draft about \\\"{topic}\\\" using these oral history accounts.\\n\\nAccounts:\\n{accounts_json}\\n\\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:\\n- USE THE ACTUAL PASSAGES EXTENSIVELY as evidence - quote liberally to support your analysis.\\n- Convert spoken language to written language: fix grammar, remove filler words, but PRESERVE the veteran's authentic voice and specific terminology.\\n- Use the passages as primary source evidence throughout your analysis.\\n\\nWrite in a scholarly style that:\\n1. Opens with a thesis or analytical framework\\n2. Supports arguments with extensive evidence from the actual accounts - quote liberally\\n3. Uses formal citations like (Rolfes, Response 014) for verbatim quotes\\n4. For passages slightly edited for written flow, use (Rolfes, Response 014, adapted)\\n5. Analyzes patterns and themes by comparing actual quotes from different veterans\\n6. Acknowledges limitations of the sources\\n7. Draws careful conclusions supported by evidence from the passages\\n\\nThe draft should use the veterans' actual words as evidence throughout, not just summarize them.\\n\\nTarget length: decide on a suitable number of words\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n}\\n\\n\\nclass DraftWriter:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Generates first-draft narrative text from oral history passages.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    \\n    def __init__(self, client: LLMClient):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Initialize draft writer.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            client: LLM client to use\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self.client = client\\n    \\n    def generate_draft(\\n        self, \\n        passages: List[Dict[str, Any]], \\n        style: str = \\\"narrative\\\",\\n        topic: str = \\\"\\\"\\n    ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Generate a first-draft narrative from passages.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            passages: List of passage dicts with veteran_id, veteran_name, response_id, response\\n            style: Writing style - \\\"narrative\\\", \\\"documentary\\\", or \\\"academic\\\"\\n            topic: Topic/title for the draft\\n            \\n        Returns:\\n            Dict with \\\"draft\\\" text and metadata\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if style not in DRAFT_PROMPT_TEMPLATES:\\n            style = \\\"narrative\\\"\\n        \\n        # Prepare accounts for the prompt\\n        # Include FULL original text of each passage - no truncation\\n        accounts = []\\n        for p in passages:\\n            response = p[\\\"response\\\"]\\n            \\n            # Get summary if available\\n            summary = \\\"\\\"\\n            if response.extracted:\\n                summary = response.extracted.summary\\n            \\n            # Include FULL response text - no truncation\\n            # The LLM needs the complete passages to quote from them extensively\\n            accounts.append({\\n                \\\"veteran_name\\\": p[\\\"veteran_name\\\"],\\n                \\\"veteran_id\\\": p[\\\"veteran_id\\\"],\\n                \\\"response_id\\\": p[\\\"response_id\\\"],\\n                \\\"interviewer_question\\\": response.interviewer,  # Full question, not truncated\\n                \\\"summary\\\": summary,\\n                \\\"text\\\": response.veteran  # Full passage text - no truncation\\n            })\\n        \\n        prompt = DRAFT_PROMPT_TEMPLATES[style].format(\\n            topic=topic,\\n            accounts_json=json.dumps(accounts, indent=2)\\n        )\\n        \\n        # Increase max_tokens to allow for more extensive quoting of original passages\\n        draft_text = self.client.complete(\\n            prompt=prompt,\\n            system=DRAFT_SYSTEM_PROMPT,\\n            max_tokens=4096  # Increased to allow for more extensive quoting\\n        )\\n        \\n        return {\\n            \\\"draft\\\": draft_text,\\n            \\\"style\\\": style,\\n            \\\"topic\\\": topic,\\n            \\\"source_count\\\": len(passages)\\n        }\\n\\n\\nclass NarrativeSynthesizer:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Synthesizes high-level narratives across one or more veterans.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    \\n    def __init__(self, client: LLMClient):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Initialize synthesizer.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            client: LLM client to use\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self.client = client\\n\\n    def synthesize_profile(self, veteran: Veteran) -> VeteranProfile:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Generate a high-level profile for a single veteran.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            veteran: The veteran to synthesize\\n            \\n        Returns:\\n            A VeteranProfile object\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        # We reuse the preparation logic from VeteranSynthesizer\\n        vs = VeteranSynthesizer(self.client)\\n        extractions_json = vs._prepare_extractions(veteran.responses)\\n        \\n        prompt = PROFILE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE.format(\\n            veteran_name=veteran.name,\\n            extractions_json=extractions_json\\n        )\\n        \\n        from datetime import datetime\\n        \\n        try:\\n            data = self.client.complete_json(\\n                prompt=prompt,\\n                system=SYNTHESIS_SYSTEM_PROMPT,\\n                max_tokens=4096\\n            )\\n            \\n            thematic_strengths = []\\n            for ts in data.get(\\\"thematic_strengths\\\", []):\\n                try:\\n                    strength = WritingPotential(ts.get(\\\"strength\\\", \\\"low\\\"))\\n                except ValueError:\\n                    strength = WritingPotential.LOW\\n                    \\n                thematic_strengths.append(ThematicStrength(\\n                    theme=ts.get(\\\"theme\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                    strength=strength,\\n                    summary=ts.get(\\\"summary\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                    response_ids=ts.get(\\\"response_ids\\\", [])\\n                ))\\n            \\n            return VeteranProfile(\\n                overview=data.get(\\\"overview\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                narrative_style=data.get(\\\"narrative_style\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                thematic_strengths=thematic_strengths,\\n                key_entities=data.get(\\\"key_entities\\\", []),\\n                writing_advice=data.get(\\\"writing_advice\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                last_updated=datetime.now().strftime(\\\"%Y-%m-NaN %H:%M:%S\\\")\\n            )\\n        except Exception as e:\\n            # Return a basic profile with error info\\n            return VeteranProfile(\\n                overview=f\\\"Synthesis failed: {str(e)}\\\",\\n                narrative_style=\\\"Unknown\\\",\\n                thematic_strengths=[],\\n                key_entities=[],\\n                writing_advice=\\\"Try re-synthesizing.\\\",\\n                last_updated=datetime.now().strftime(\\\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\\\")\\n            )\\n\\n    def synthesize_topic(self, query: str, hits: List[SearchHit]) -> str:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Synthesize multiple accounts regarding a specific topic.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            query: The topic query\\n            hits: Search results to synthesize\\n            \\n        Returns:\\n            A markdown-formatted synthesis\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        accounts = []\\n        for hit in hits:\\n            # Send up to 3000 characters per response to allow for meaningful weaving\\n            raw_text = hit.response.veteran\\n            if len(raw_text) > 3000:\\n                raw_text = raw_text[:3000] + \\\"...\\\"\\n                \\n            accounts.append({\\n                \\\"veteran_id\\\": hit.veteran_id,\\n                \\\"veteran_name\\\": hit.veteran_name,\\n                \\\"response_id\\\": hit.response_id,\\n                \\\"summary\\\": hit.response.extracted.summary if hit.response.extracted else \\\"No summary available.\\\",\\n                \\\"text\\\": raw_text\\n            })\\n            \\n        prompt = TOPIC_SYNTHESIS_PROMPT_TEMPLATE.format(\\n            query=query,\\n            accounts_json=json.dumps(accounts, indent=2)\\n        )\\n        \\n        return self.client.complete(\\n            prompt=prompt,\\n            system=TOPIC_SYNTHESIS_SYSTEM_PROMPT,\\n            max_tokens=4096\\n        )\\n\",\"file_size_bytes\":23491,\"content_length\":23491}"}],"structuredContent":{"result":"{\"success\":true,\"file_path\":\"/Users/happyhawking/Documents/Projects/Current/writer/src/llm/synthesizer.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nVeteran profile synthesizer for the Oral History Research System.\\n\\nUses LLM to synthesize a veteran's timeline, relationships, and notable stories\\nfrom all their extracted response metadata.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any, Optional\\nimport json\\n\\nfrom .client import LLMClient\\nfrom ..models import (\\n    Response, Veteran, TimelineEvent, Relationship, \\n    NotableStory, VerificationItem, DatePrecision, Confidence, WritingPotential,\\n    VeteranProfile, ThematicStrength, SearchHit\\n)\\n\\n\\nSYNTHESIS_SYSTEM_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are synthesizing a WWII veteran's complete oral history interview for book research.\\nYour task is to create a comprehensive profile that will help a researcher understand this veteran's story.\\nBe meticulous about dates, names, and connections. Flag anything ambiguous for verification.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nPROFILE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE = \\\"\\\"\\\"Synthesize a high-level researcher's profile for this WWII veteran.\\nAnalyze their entire interview and identify their strongest narrative themes, writing potential, and key entities.\\n\\nVeteran: {veteran_name}\\nSummary of all responses:\\n{extractions_json}\\n\\nCreate a profile with:\\n1. Overview: A 3-4 sentence summary of who they were and their main contribution to the war effort.\\n2. Narrative Style: Describe how they tell their story (e.g., \\\"Emotionally detached but technically precise\\\", \\\"Vivid storyteller with strong sensory details\\\", \\\"Focused on interpersonal relationships\\\").\\n3. Thematic Strengths: Identify 3-5 key themes where this veteran provides high-quality information. For each:\\n   - theme: e.g., \\\"Combat\\\", \\\"Training\\\", \\\"Logistics\\\", \\\"Home Front\\\", \\\"POW Life\\\"\\n   - strength: \\\"high\\\" | \\\"medium\\\" | \\\"low\\\"\\n   - summary: Why is this a strength? What specific types of details do they provide?\\n   - response_ids: Which responses support this theme?\\n4. Key Entities: List the 5-10 most important locations, units, or terms associated with this veteran.\\n5. Writing Advice: Advice to the author on how best to use this veteran's testimony in a book.\\n\\nReturn as JSON:\\n{{\\n  \\\"overview\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n  \\\"narrative_style\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n  \\\"thematic_strengths\\\": [\\n    {{\\n      \\\"theme\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n      \\\"strength\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n      \\\"response_ids\\\": [...]\\n    }}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"key_entities\\\": [...],\\n  \\\"writing_advice\\\": \\\"...\\\"\\n}}\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nTOPIC_SYNTHESIS_SYSTEM_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are a master WWII historian and book researcher.\\nYour task is to synthesize multiple accounts from different veterans into a single, cohesive narrative for a book.\\nHighlight areas of consensus and unique perspectives. Always cite your sources using [VeteranID:ResponseID].\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nTOPIC_SYNTHESIS_PROMPT_TEMPLATE = \\\"\\\"\\\"Synthesize the following accounts regarding the topic: \\\"{query}\\\"\\n\\nAccounts:\\n{accounts_json}\\n\\nCreate a narrative synthesis that:\\n1. Provides a cohesive 3-5 paragraph overview of the topic based on these specific accounts.\\n2. WEAVE IN ORIGINAL PASSAGES: Use direct quotes and specific terminology from the veterans' own words. Instead of saying \\\"He described the cold\\\", say \\\"He described how it was '20 below zero with a foot and a half of snow' [veteran:001]\\\".\\n3. Go beyond high-level summaries; use specific descriptions of equipment, weather, emotions, and vivid sensory details from the accounts.\\n4. Highlights unique details that only one veteran mentioned.\\n5. Notes any contradictions or different perspectives on the same event.\\n6. Uses citations like [jarussi_hugo_victor:012] throughout the text.\\n\\nStructure your response with a clear title and sections.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nSYNTHESIS_PROMPT_TEMPLATE = \\\"\\\"\\\"Synthesize this WWII veteran's interview data into a comprehensive profile.\\n\\nVeteran: {veteran_name}\\nNumber of responses: {response_count}\\n\\nHere is the extracted metadata from each response:\\n\\n{extractions_json}\\n\\nCreate a synthesis with:\\n\\n## 1. Timeline\\nCreate a chronological timeline of events. For each event:\\n- date: as specific as possible, or approximate with ~\\n- date_precision: \\\"year\\\" | \\\"month\\\" | \\\"day\\\" | \\\"approximate\\\"\\n- event: description\\n- confidence: \\\"stated\\\" (veteran explicitly said this) | \\\"inferred\\\" (derived from context) | \\\"approximate\\\" (vague terms)\\n- response_ids: list of response IDs that support this event\\n- note: any ambiguity or need for verification (null if clear)\\n\\n## 2. Relationships\\nIdentify all people mentioned:\\n- Consolidate name variants (e.g., \\\"Tip\\\" and \\\"Tipton\\\" are likely the same person)\\n- id: slug identifier for this person\\n- canonical: best/most complete name version\\n- names: all variants found\\n- role: if determinable\\n- context: how they relate to the veteran\\n- response_ids: where they appear\\n\\n## 3. Notable Stories\\nIdentify the TOP 5-10 stories most valuable for a book:\\n- id: slug identifier\\n- title: short, descriptive title\\n- summary: 2-3 sentence summary\\n- response_ids: which responses contain this story\\n- writing_potential: should all be \\\"high\\\"\\n- writing_note: why this story matters (drama, humor, humanity, unique detail, action, sensory detail)\\n\\nLook for:\\n- Action sequences with tension\\n- Moments of humanity amid war\\n- Vivid sensory details (food, weather, sounds, smells)\\n- Humor or irony\\n- Emotional turning points\\n- Unique perspectives not commonly recorded\\n- Named characters and specific places\\n\\n## 4. Verification Needed\\nFlag anything that:\\n- Has conflicting dates\\n- Is ambiguous about locations or people\\n- Would benefit from cross-referencing with unit histories\\n- The veteran expressed uncertainty about\\n\\nReturn as JSON:\\n{{\\n  \\\"timeline\\\": [...],\\n  \\\"relationships\\\": [...],\\n  \\\"notable_stories\\\": [...],\\n  \\\"verification_needed\\\": [...]\\n}}\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass VeteranSynthesizer:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Synthesizes veteran profiles from response extractions.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    \\n    def __init__(self, client: LLMClient):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Initialize synthesizer.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            client: LLM client to use\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self.client = client\\n    \\n    def _prepare_extractions(self, responses: List[Response]) -> str:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Prepare extractions for LLM prompt.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            responses: Responses with extractions\\n            \\n        Returns:\\n            JSON string of extractions\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        extractions = []\\n        \\n        for r in responses:\\n            if r.extracted:\\n                extractions.append({\\n                    \\\"response_id\\\": r.id,\\n                    \\\"interviewer_question\\\": r.interviewer[:200] + \\\"...\\\" if len(r.interviewer) > 200 else r.interviewer,\\n                    \\\"summary\\\": r.extracted.summary,\\n                    \\\"dates\\\": [{\\\"value\\\": d.value, \\\"context\\\": d.context, \\\"precision\\\": d.precision} for d in r.extracted.dates],\\n                    \\\"locations\\\": r.extracted.locations,\\n                    \\\"people\\\": [{\\\"name\\\": p.name, \\\"role\\\": p.role, \\\"context\\\": p.context} for p in r.extracted.people],\\n                    \\\"units\\\": r.extracted.units,\\n                    \\\"events\\\": r.extracted.events,\\n                    \\\"topics\\\": r.extracted.topics,\\n                    \\\"writing_potential\\\": r.extracted.writing_potential.value,\\n                    \\\"writing_note\\\": r.extracted.writing_note,\\n                })\\n        \\n        return json.dumps(extractions, indent=2)\\n    \\n    def synthesize(self, veteran: Veteran) -> Veteran:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Synthesize timeline, relationships, and stories from responses.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            veteran: Veteran with responses and extractions\\n            \\n        Returns:\\n            Updated veteran with synthesized data\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if not veteran.responses:\\n            return veteran\\n        \\n        extractions_json = self._prepare_extractions(veteran.responses)\\n        \\n        prompt = SYNTHESIS_PROMPT_TEMPLATE.format(\\n            veteran_name=veteran.name,\\n            response_count=len(veteran.responses),\\n            extractions_json=extractions_json\\n        )\\n        \\n        try:\\n            data = self.client.complete_json(\\n                prompt=prompt,\\n                system=SYNTHESIS_SYSTEM_PROMPT,\\n                max_tokens=8192\\n            )\\n            \\n            # Parse timeline\\n            timeline = []\\n            for t in data.get(\\\"timeline\\\", []):\\n                if isinstance(t, dict):\\n                    # Parse date precision\\n                    dp_str = t.get(\\\"date_precision\\\", \\\"approximate\\\")\\n                    try:\\n                        date_precision = DatePrecision(dp_str)\\n                    except ValueError:\\n                        date_precision = DatePrecision.APPROXIMATE\\n                    \\n                    # Parse confidence\\n                    conf_str = t.get(\\\"confidence\\\", \\\"inferred\\\")\\n                    try:\\n                        confidence = Confidence(conf_str)\\n                    except ValueError:\\n                        confidence = Confidence.INFERRED\\n                    \\n                    timeline.append(TimelineEvent(\\n                        date=t.get(\\\"date\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        date_precision=date_precision,\\n                        event=t.get(\\\"event\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        confidence=confidence,\\n                        response_ids=t.get(\\\"response_ids\\\", []),\\n                        note=t.get(\\\"note\\\")\\n                    ))\\n            \\n            # Parse relationships\\n            relationships = []\\n            for r in data.get(\\\"relationships\\\", []):\\n                if isinstance(r, dict):\\n                    relationships.append(Relationship(\\n                        id=r.get(\\\"id\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        names=r.get(\\\"names\\\", [r.get(\\\"canonical\\\", \\\"\\\")]),\\n                        canonical=r.get(\\\"canonical\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        role=r.get(\\\"role\\\"),\\n                        context=r.get(\\\"context\\\"),\\n                        response_ids=r.get(\\\"response_ids\\\", []),\\n                        linked_veteran=r.get(\\\"linked_veteran\\\")\\n                    ))\\n            \\n            # Parse notable stories\\n            notable_stories = []\\n            for s in data.get(\\\"notable_stories\\\", []):\\n                if isinstance(s, dict):\\n                    # Parse writing potential\\n                    wp_str = s.get(\\\"writing_potential\\\", \\\"high\\\")\\n                    try:\\n                        writing_potential = WritingPotential(wp_str)\\n                    except ValueError:\\n                        writing_potential = WritingPotential.HIGH\\n                    \\n                    notable_stories.append(NotableStory(\\n                        id=s.get(\\\"id\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        title=s.get(\\\"title\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        summary=s.get(\\\"summary\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        response_ids=s.get(\\\"response_ids\\\", []),\\n                        writing_potential=writing_potential,\\n                        writing_note=s.get(\\\"writing_note\\\")\\n                    ))\\n            \\n            # Parse verification needed\\n            verification_needed = []\\n            for v in data.get(\\\"verification_needed\\\", []):\\n                if isinstance(v, dict):\\n                    verification_needed.append(VerificationItem(\\n                        issue=v.get(\\\"issue\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        detail=v.get(\\\"detail\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                        response_ids=v.get(\\\"response_ids\\\", [])\\n                    ))\\n            \\n            # Update veteran\\n            veteran.timeline = timeline\\n            veteran.relationships = relationships\\n            veteran.notable_stories = notable_stories\\n            veteran.verification_needed = verification_needed\\n            \\n            # Also generate narrative profile\\n            narrative_synth = NarrativeSynthesizer(self.client)\\n            veteran.profile = narrative_synth.synthesize_profile(veteran)\\n            \\n        except (json.JSONDecodeError, KeyError) as e:\\n            # Add error to verification\\n            veteran.verification_needed = [\\n                VerificationItem(\\n                    issue=\\\"Synthesis error\\\",\\n                    detail=f\\\"LLM synthesis failed: {str(e)}\\\",\\n                    response_ids=[]\\n                )\\n            ]\\n        \\n        return veteran\\n    \\n    def extract_basic_info(self, responses: List[Response]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Extract basic veteran info (unit, rank, service dates) from responses.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            responses: Responses with extractions\\n            \\n        Returns:\\n            Dict with unit, rank, service_dates\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        units = set()\\n        ranks = set()\\n        dates = []\\n        \\n        for r in responses:\\n            if r.extracted:\\n                for unit in r.extracted.units:\\n                    units.add(unit)\\n                # Look for rank in topics or summary\\n                if \\\"rank\\\" in (r.extracted.summary or \\\"\\\").lower():\\n                    # Try to extract rank\\n                    pass\\n        \\n        return {\\n            \\\"unit\\\": list(units)[0] if units else None,\\n            \\\"rank\\\": list(ranks)[0] if ranks else None,\\n        }\\n\\n\\nDRAFT_SYSTEM_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are a skilled historical writer helping to create first-draft narrative text from WWII oral history interviews.\\nYour task is to use the actual passages from veterans' accounts to tell the story, converting spoken language to written language while preserving their authentic voice.\\nAlways include inline citations in the format (VeteranName, Response XXX) to attribute quotes and information.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nDRAFT_PROMPT_TEMPLATES = {\\n    \\\"narrative\\\": \\\"\\\"\\\"Write a narrative first-draft about \\\"{topic}\\\" using these oral history accounts.\\n\\nAccounts:\\n{accounts_json}\\n\\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:\\n- USE THE ACTUAL PASSAGES EXTENSIVELY - don't just summarize. Quote liberally from the accounts.\\n- Convert spoken language to written language: fix grammar, remove filler words (\\\"um\\\", \\\"you know\\\"), smooth transitions, but PRESERVE the veteran's authentic voice and specific details.\\n- Weave the passages together to tell the story - use the veterans' own words as the foundation of your narrative.\\n- When a passage needs slight tweaking for written flow, make minimal edits that preserve meaning and voice.\\n\\nWrite in a compelling, human narrative style that:\\n1. Opens with a strong hook using one of the actual passages\\n2. Weaves the veterans' actual words throughout - quote extensively, don't paraphrase\\n3. Uses direct quotes with citations like (Rolfes, Response 014) for verbatim quotes\\n4. For passages you've slightly edited for written flow, use citations like (Rolfes, Response 014, adapted)\\n5. Creates vivid scenes using the sensory details from the actual accounts\\n6. Maintains chronological or thematic flow by connecting the passages\\n7. Ends with reflection or significance using the veterans' own words when possible\\n\\nThe draft should feel like the veterans are telling the story through their own words, with minimal narrative scaffolding.\\n\\nTarget length: decide on a suitable number of words for a polished narrative prose.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"documentary\\\": \\\"\\\"\\\"Write a documentary-style draft about \\\"{topic}\\\" using these oral history accounts.\\n\\nAccounts:\\n{accounts_json}\\n\\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:\\n- USE THE ACTUAL PASSAGES EXTENSIVELY - quote liberally, don't summarize.\\n- Convert spoken language to written language: fix grammar, remove filler words, smooth transitions, but PRESERVE the veteran's authentic voice.\\n- Let the veterans' words tell the story - use extensive direct quotes with minimal editorial commentary.\\n\\nWrite in an objective, journalistic style that:\\n1. Presents facts and testimonies in a balanced way using the actual accounts\\n2. Uses extensive direct quotes with citations like (Rolfes, Response 014)\\n3. For passages slightly edited for written flow, use (Rolfes, Response 014, adapted)\\n4. Provides minimal context between quotes - let the quotes do the work\\n5. Acknowledges different perspectives by showing contrasting quotes\\n6. Lets the veterans' words speak for themselves - quote extensively\\n7. Maintains objectivity while honoring the subjects\\n\\nThe draft should be primarily the veterans' own words with minimal narrative intervention.\\n\\nTarget length: decide on a suitable number of words\\n\\\"\\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"academic\\\": \\\"\\\"\\\"Write an academic-style draft about \\\"{topic}\\\" using these oral history accounts.\\n\\nAccounts:\\n{accounts_json}\\n\\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:\\n- USE THE ACTUAL PASSAGES EXTENSIVELY as evidence - quote liberally to support your analysis.\\n- Convert spoken language to written language: fix grammar, remove filler words, but PRESERVE the veteran's authentic voice and specific terminology.\\n- Use the passages as primary source evidence throughout your analysis.\\n\\nWrite in a scholarly style that:\\n1. Opens with a thesis or analytical framework\\n2. Supports arguments with extensive evidence from the actual accounts - quote liberally\\n3. Uses formal citations like (Rolfes, Response 014) for verbatim quotes\\n4. For passages slightly edited for written flow, use (Rolfes, Response 014, adapted)\\n5. Analyzes patterns and themes by comparing actual quotes from different veterans\\n6. Acknowledges limitations of the sources\\n7. Draws careful conclusions supported by evidence from the passages\\n\\nThe draft should use the veterans' actual words as evidence throughout, not just summarize them.\\n\\nTarget length: decide on a suitable number of words\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n}\\n\\n\\nclass DraftWriter:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Generates first-draft narrative text from oral history passages.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    \\n    def __init__(self, client: LLMClient):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Initialize draft writer.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            client: LLM client to use\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self.client = client\\n    \\n    def generate_draft(\\n        self, \\n        passages: List[Dict[str, Any]], \\n        style: str = \\\"narrative\\\",\\n        topic: str = \\\"\\\"\\n    ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Generate a first-draft narrative from passages.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            passages: List of passage dicts with veteran_id, veteran_name, response_id, response\\n            style: Writing style - \\\"narrative\\\", \\\"documentary\\\", or \\\"academic\\\"\\n            topic: Topic/title for the draft\\n            \\n        Returns:\\n            Dict with \\\"draft\\\" text and metadata\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if style not in DRAFT_PROMPT_TEMPLATES:\\n            style = \\\"narrative\\\"\\n        \\n        # Prepare accounts for the prompt\\n        # Include FULL original text of each passage - no truncation\\n        accounts = []\\n        for p in passages:\\n            response = p[\\\"response\\\"]\\n            \\n            # Get summary if available\\n            summary = \\\"\\\"\\n            if response.extracted:\\n                summary = response.extracted.summary\\n            \\n            # Include FULL response text - no truncation\\n            # The LLM needs the complete passages to quote from them extensively\\n            accounts.append({\\n                \\\"veteran_name\\\": p[\\\"veteran_name\\\"],\\n                \\\"veteran_id\\\": p[\\\"veteran_id\\\"],\\n                \\\"response_id\\\": p[\\\"response_id\\\"],\\n                \\\"interviewer_question\\\": response.interviewer,  # Full question, not truncated\\n                \\\"summary\\\": summary,\\n                \\\"text\\\": response.veteran  # Full passage text - no truncation\\n            })\\n        \\n        prompt = DRAFT_PROMPT_TEMPLATES[style].format(\\n            topic=topic,\\n            accounts_json=json.dumps(accounts, indent=2)\\n        )\\n        \\n        # Increase max_tokens to allow for more extensive quoting of original passages\\n        draft_text = self.client.complete(\\n            prompt=prompt,\\n            system=DRAFT_SYSTEM_PROMPT,\\n            max_tokens=4096  # Increased to allow for more extensive quoting\\n        )\\n        \\n        return {\\n            \\\"draft\\\": draft_text,\\n            \\\"style\\\": style,\\n            \\\"topic\\\": topic,\\n            \\\"source_count\\\": len(passages)\\n        }\\n\\n\\nclass NarrativeSynthesizer:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Synthesizes high-level narratives across one or more veterans.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    \\n    def __init__(self, client: LLMClient):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Initialize synthesizer.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            client: LLM client to use\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self.client = client\\n\\n    def synthesize_profile(self, veteran: Veteran) -> VeteranProfile:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Generate a high-level profile for a single veteran.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            veteran: The veteran to synthesize\\n            \\n        Returns:\\n            A VeteranProfile object\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        # We reuse the preparation logic from VeteranSynthesizer\\n        vs = VeteranSynthesizer(self.client)\\n        extractions_json = vs._prepare_extractions(veteran.responses)\\n        \\n        prompt = PROFILE_PROMPT_TEMPLATE.format(\\n            veteran_name=veteran.name,\\n            extractions_json=extractions_json\\n        )\\n        \\n        from datetime import datetime\\n        \\n        try:\\n            data = self.client.complete_json(\\n                prompt=prompt,\\n                system=SYNTHESIS_SYSTEM_PROMPT,\\n                max_tokens=4096\\n            )\\n            \\n            thematic_strengths = []\\n            for ts in data.get(\\\"thematic_strengths\\\", []):\\n                try:\\n                    strength = WritingPotential(ts.get(\\\"strength\\\", \\\"low\\\"))\\n                except ValueError:\\n                    strength = WritingPotential.LOW\\n                    \\n                thematic_strengths.append(ThematicStrength(\\n                    theme=ts.get(\\\"theme\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                    strength=strength,\\n                    summary=ts.get(\\\"summary\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                    response_ids=ts.get(\\\"response_ids\\\", [])\\n                ))\\n            \\n            return VeteranProfile(\\n                overview=data.get(\\\"overview\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                narrative_style=data.get(\\\"narrative_style\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                thematic_strengths=thematic_strengths,\\n                key_entities=data.get(\\\"key_entities\\\", []),\\n                writing_advice=data.get(\\\"writing_advice\\\", \\\"\\\"),\\n                last_updated=datetime.now().strftime(\\\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\\\")\\n            )\\n        except Exception as e:\\n            # Return a basic profile with error info\\n            return VeteranProfile(\\n                overview=f\\\"Synthesis failed: {str(e)}\\\",\\n                narrative_style=\\\"Unknown\\\",\\n                thematic_strengths=[],\\n                key_entities=[],\\n                writing_advice=\\\"Try re-synthesizing.\\\",\\n                last_updated=datetime.now().strftime(\\\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\\\")\\n            )\\n\\n    def synthesize_topic(self, query: str, hits: List[SearchHit]) -> str:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Synthesize multiple accounts regarding a specific topic.\\n        \\n        Args:\\n            query: The topic query\\n            hits: Search results to synthesize\\n            \\n        Returns:\\n            A markdown-formatted synthesis\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        accounts = []\\n        for hit in hits:\\n            # Send up to 3000 characters per response to allow for meaningful weaving\\n            raw_text = hit.response.veteran\\n            if len(raw_text) > 3000:\\n                raw_text = raw_text[:3000] + \\\"...\\\"\\n                \\n            accounts.append({\\n                \\\"veteran_id\\\": hit.veteran_id,\\n                \\\"veteran_name\\\": hit.veteran_name,\\n                \\\"response_id\\\": hit.response_id,\\n                \\\"summary\\\": hit.response.extracted.summary if hit.response.extracted else \\\"No summary available.\\\",\\n                \\\"text\\\": raw_text\\n            })\\n            \\n        prompt = TOPIC_SYNTHESIS_PROMPT_TEMPLATE.format(\\n            query=query,\\n            accounts_json=json.dumps(accounts, indent=2)\\n        )\\n        \\n        return self.client.complete(\\n            prompt=prompt,\\n            system=TOPIC_SYNTHESIS_SYSTEM_PROMPT,\\n            max_tokens=4096\\n        )\\n\",\"file_size_bytes\":23491,\"content_length\":23491}"},"isError":false}} %o
