2025-12-21T16:45:53.648Z [iterm2] [info] Message from server: {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":31,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"file_path\": \"/Users/happyhawking/Documents/Projects/Current/writer/README.md\",\n  \"content\": \"\\n# Read the full passage\\noralhistory view rolfes_john_w 023\\n\\n# Assign it to your chapter\\noralhistory annotate rolfes_john_w 023 --chapter 3 --note \\\"Opening scene\\\"\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Commands\\n\\n### Getting Started\\n\\n| Command | What it does |\\n|---------|--------------|\\n| `oralhistory init` | Create a new project |\\n| `oralhistory ingest <file> --veteran \\\"Name\\\"` | Parse and import a transcript |\\n| `oralhistory veterans` | List everyone in your project |\\n\\n### Finding Material\\n\\n| Command | What it does |\\n|---------|--------------|\\n| `oralhistory search \\\"query\\\"` | Semantic search across all veterans |\\n| `oralhistory entity \\\"Patton\\\"` | Find who mentions a specific person/place/unit |\\n| `oralhistory topic \\\"Bastogne\\\"` | AI-synthesized narrative across all veterans |\\n\\n**Search examples:**\\n```bash\\n# Find passages about tank combat\\noralhistory search \\\"tank combat destroyed\\\"\\n\\n# Find only high-potential passages\\noralhistory search \\\"winter cold\\\" --potential high\\n\\n# Search within one veteran\\noralhistory search \\\"training\\\" --veteran rolfes_john_w\\n\\n# Find everyone who mentions a specific person\\noralhistory entity \\\"Gruber\\\"\\n\\n# Find all location references\\noralhistory entity \\\"Rhine\\\" --type location\\n```\\n\\n### Understanding a Veteran\\n\\n| Command | What it does |\\n|---------|--------------|\\n| `oralhistory veteran <id>` | Full profile: timeline, relationships, notable stories |\\n| `oralhistory veteran <id> --timeline` | Just the chronology |\\n| `oralhistory profile <id>` | AI-generated \\\"researcher's brief\\\" |\\n| `oralhistory view <id> <response>` | Read a full response untruncated |\\n| `oralhistory context <id> <response>` | See surrounding Q&A for context |\\n\\n**Example workflow:**\\n```bash\\n# Get overview of this veteran\\noralhistory veteran jarussi_hugo\\n\\n# See their chronological story\\noralhistory veteran jarussi_hugo --timeline\\n\\n# Get the AI's take on their narrative strengths\\noralhistory profile jarussi_hugo\\n\\n# Found interesting response #14 in search? Read the full thing\\noralhistory view jarussi_hugo 014\\n\\n# What led to that answer? What came next?\\noralhistory context jarussi_hugo 014 --before 2 --after 2\\n```\\n\\n### Organizing Your Research\\n\\n| Command | What it does |\\n|---------|--------------|\\n| `oralhistory annotate <id> <resp> --chapter N` | Assign response to a chapter |\\n| `oralhistory annotate <id> <resp> --note \\\"text\\\"` | Add your notes |\\n| `oralhistory annotate <id> <resp> --flag \\\"name\\\"` | Add a custom flag |\\n| `oralhistory chapter N` | See everything assigned to chapter N |\\n| `oralhistory annotations --chapter N` | List all chapter N annotations |\\n\\n**Example workflow:**\\n```bash\\n# Found a great passage \\u2014 assign it\\noralhistory annotate rolfes_john_w 023 \\\\\\n  --chapter 3 \\\\\\n  --note \\\"Great opening \\u2014 sensory detail about the cold\\\"\\n\\n# Later, review your chapter material\\noralhistory chapter 3\\n\\n# Find all passages you've flagged\\noralhistory annotations --flags\\n```\\n\\n### Synthesis & Writing\\n\\n| Command | What it does |\\n\",\n  \"file_size_bytes\": 11832,\n  \"content_length\": 2928\n}"}],"structuredContent":{"result":"{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"file_path\": \"/Users/happyhawking/Documents/Projects/Current/writer/README.md\",\n  \"content\": \"\\n# Read the full passage\\noralhistory view rolfes_john_w 023\\n\\n# Assign it to your chapter\\noralhistory annotate rolfes_john_w 023 --chapter 3 --note \\\"Opening scene\\\"\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Commands\\n\\n### Getting Started\\n\\n| Command | What it does |\\n|----